ew/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/31/code.py:36:#      maroon} has count 4 instead, so it matches the red count-4 rule and stamps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/9/code.py:30:#      only sprite hits: enemy fire recolors the whole target sprite to maroon (9), while friendly fire\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/9/code.py:37:#        * D9 alone:   that same mixed-team pair would become maroon(9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/9/code.py:201:    - If a landing cell lies on a sprite, only enemy-team shooters matter: if at least one incoming projectile comes from the opposite team, recolor the whole target sprite to maroon (9); friendly fire leaves it unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/9/code.py:202:    - If a landing cell is empty background, paint that one cell by the number of projectiles that arrived there: 1 -> maroon (9), 2 -> blue (1), 3 -> red (2), 4 -> green (3), then continue through the visible non-background palette while skipping the background color 7.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:73:#    - Colors keep the original semantics: original sprite color is arbitrary but uniform; maroon 9\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:203:    - If that landing cell lies on another sprite, recolor the entire hit sprite to maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:204:    - If multiple projectiles land on the same empty background cell, paint it blue (1); otherwise a lone empty-background landing paints maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/4/code.py:17:#   若通道列是 [c0,c1,c2,c3,c4]，第 1 层交换 (c0,c1),(c2,c3)，第 2 层交换 (c1,c2),(c3,c4)，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/4/code.py:34:# - 通道间距固定为 4。这样既能容纳 45 度对角线，又能在 26x26 以内放下 3 层交换带、上下 token 和偶发 9-rect。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/4/code.py:267:      diagonal swap bands, optional maroon pass-through rectangles on straight vertical subsegments, and colored\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/4/code.py:275:    - A maroon rectangle still acts as a chamber that passes a wire straight through from one face to the opposite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/5/code.py:20:#      “solid / X 是两类源态”，再看出“solid 的被传输部分比 X 通道多一个中心像素”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/5/code.py:22:#    - 继续保留 4-5 条通道、非恒等置换、0-3 个 9-矩形与跨线标记，避免任务退化成直接上下复制。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/5/code.py:49:#    - 假设每个颜色只对应一条通道，不会出现同色源 token 争用同一导线分量；generator 继续为每条通道分配独立颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/21/code.py:15:#      Every background cell on that path is painted maroon 9, and the entire struck\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/21/code.py:53:#      geometry, then see a straight maroon trail stop exactly when it reaches a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/21/code.py:54:#      pre-existing colored bar. Hit bars change to maroon while untouched bars keep\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/21/code.py:63:#    - Sprite color and line colors exclude 9 so the added maroon effects remain easy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/21/code.py:67:#    - Output color changes are structurally tied to geometry: maroon 9 means either\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/21/code.py:289:      reaches a colored line cell. Every background cell before that hit is painted maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/21/code.py:291:      cell to maroon (9). Triangles do not change, and rays that never meet a line do nothing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/28/code.py:402:    \"\"\"Attempt to replace a wire segment block with a maroon pass-through rectangle.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/1/code.py:27:#        even when those L-shapes are yellow or maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/19/code.py:21:# - Output paints every in-flight background cell on that fused path in maroon 9.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/19/code.py:237:    - Paint every non-endpoint background cell on that arc maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/19/code.py:238:    - At the final cell, keep the original endpoint semantics: a hit sprite is recolored entirely to maroon (9), a shared empty landing cell becomes blue (1), and a lone empty landing cell becomes maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/4/code.py:21:#      path cells shown in maroon 9.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/4/code.py:27:#      cross centered at (8,8) while the rest of both trajectories stay maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/4/code.py:36:#    - Only two effect colors are used: maroon 9 for ordinary trail / lone landing /\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/4/code.py:41:#      learner sees both maroon-only trajectories and blue collision crosses together.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/4/code.py:52:#    - Explosion crosses now coexist with trails. Write order matters: maroon trails are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/4/code.py:65:#    - A human can read direction from the maroon rays and can distinguish collision from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/4/code.py:80:#      one projectile on a background path cell -> maroon; multiple projectiles on the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/4/code.py:82:#      that sprite maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/4/code.py:176:    - The projectile occupies the whole 5-cell ray from the apex. Any path cell on background is painted maroon (9), so the full straight trajectory becomes visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/4/code.py:177:    - If the step-5 destination lies on a sprite, that entire struck sprite is recolored maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db0c5428/16/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形阵列+无空洞\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/23/code.py:17:#    - 一个具体轨迹：若顶部有 color-1 solid，连到某条通道并沿路穿过 2 个 9-rect，那么输出顶部中心\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/23/code.py:23:#    - 为了让“颜色决定分解”在少量样例里可见，我不再要求每条通道颜色互异，而是固定 4 条通道中有\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/23/code.py:38:#    - token 仍然放在 degree-1 端点外 2 格的 3x3 框中；通道列、上下 token 行、交叉行都沿用原题几何，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/23/code.py:45:#    - 解题者在单个样例里就能看到：同为 color 1 的两条通道都留下 X，而同为 color 6 的两条通道都\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/23/code.py:52:#    - 9-rect 仍然是规则矩形，而且只嵌在竖直线段里，便于人眼数出“这条路径经过了几个 maroon 块”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/23/code.py:56:#    - 源颜色只用两种，并且每种颜色都在样例内重复，避免把“颜色决定分解”退化成四条通道各不相同的孤例。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/5/code.py:66:#      always grey (5); lone landings and hit sprites are maroon (9); shared bg landings are blue (1).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/5/code.py:297:    - If the first obstruction is a sprite, recolor the entire struck sprite to maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/5/code.py:298:    - If the first obstruction is a wall, the projectile lands on the cell immediately before that wall; if no obstruction appears before leaving the grid, it lands on the last in-bounds boundary cell. Shared empty landing cells become blue (1), while lone empty landing cells become maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/13/code.py:23:#       Rationale: excluding 1 and 9 keeps the transformed maroon marks visible,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/13/code.py:66:#     after D5/3; the fused solver must collapse that branch to one maroon outcome.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/13/code.py:173:    - If a landing cell lies on a sprite, repaint that entire struck sprite maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/13/code.py:174:    - If a landing cell is empty background, paint that cell maroon (9), even when both projectiles share that same empty cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/13/code.py:176:    Key insight: The only semantic change from the parent family is the removal of the blue collision exception; on this 8x8 compressed board, both single empty impacts and double empty impacts collapse to the same maroon marker, while shape-based direction decoding stays unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/6/code.py:18:#       - 只有上下同色夹住的通道才可进入；上下异色的假走廊仍不可进入。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/6/code.py:24:#       - 某真实通道从 (r,0) 出发，先向右走 4 步，在第 5 步拐进竖走廊。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/6/code.py:37:#       会把这类真实通道误判为假走廊。这里改用“该行上下主导条带色”识别真/假，并要求假走廊的异色支撑\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/6/code.py:41:#     - 每条假走廊至少保留一个未装饰的背景格，保证 solver 能看见“上下异色夹住的通道”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/32/code.py:3:# Name: 宽通道约束+L/T形区域\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/23/code.py:331:    - Hitting a triangle recolors that entire triangle to maroon (9). Reaching an empty background stop\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/23/code.py:332:      paints that cell maroon (9), except that shared empty stops from two or more rays become blue (1).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db0c5428/10/code.py:3:# Name: 角像素编码中心+十字形空洞\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/22/code.py:31:#       B becomes solid maroon, C paints one maroon marker, D stays unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/22/code.py:33:#       B is erased to background, C still paints one maroon marker, D keeps its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/22/code.py:74:#     and maroon bg hits remain unambiguous to a human viewer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/22/code.py:162:    - If the landing cell lies on a sprite, erase the entire struck sprite to the background; if it lies on empty background, paint that cell maroon (9) for a single projectile or blue (1) for a shared collision.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/6/code.py:29:#       * Original task: the green 3-cell sprite stays present but becomes maroon 9.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/6/code.py:47:#         blue/maroon empty-impact markers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/14/code.py:21:      - original task: the green target becomes constant maroon 9\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/14/code.py:24:        not maroon 9; if red (2) and teal (8) both land on the same empty bg cell, that cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/12/code.py:13:#   into A. Original task: A would just become maroon at its old location. D4-only: A would recolor to S's color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/12/code.py:295:    - If the landing cell is empty background, paint that cell maroon (9), or blue (1) when multiple projectiles share it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/6/code.py:98:      can infer \"red/grey/teal/maroon indicate earlier to later chain slots\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/9/code.py:3:# Name: 碰撞十字形标记+path含内部障碍物\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:50:#     - 新 main() 假设 path 更接近单通道拓扑：前方通则直走，前方堵则只在左右 90 度中选。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/14/code.py:31:#         suppose a legend uses pink source 6, maroon target 9, and a 3x3 teal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/14/code.py:35:#         maroon. In this combo, the same scattered pixel becomes the stencil's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/14/code.py:36:#         center; its center cell stays maroon(9), edge cells become red(2), and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/14/code.py:49:#         maroon(9) -> red(2)    -> orange(7)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/10/code.py:42:    - 单纯把新填腔体内部加入前沿还不够；共享墙体会在 D6 擦除后变成新的通道，因此被擦掉的 boundary 也必须并入前沿。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D4/0/code.py:33:#    - Suppose legend rows say red->blue, green->yellow, yellow->maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D4/0/code.py:35:#    - Variant logic fills dst as [blue, yellow, blue, maroon].\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D9/1/code.py:3:# Change: 直角折线（rectilinear polylines），每分量0-6个转角，每色1-4个连通分量，端点垂直于边界... → T形/十字形交叉节点\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/29/code.py:23:#      orange/black lattice, and one central maroon 6x6 stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/29/code.py:32:#      union of all 2x2-tiled motifs as one maroon 6x6 mark at the canvas center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/29/code.py:67:#    - The maroon stamp remains a single centered 6x6 region, so the rest of the canvas\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/29/code.py:235:    - Composite the full-canvas layers in row-major macro-cell order so later glyph regions overwrite earlier ones, then place the 2x2-tiled union of all glyphs as a maroon 6x6 stamp at the output center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:28:#        glyph -> decode 3x3 phase tile -> tile full 16x16 lattice -> stamp 2x2 maroon glyph at center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:34:#              -> stamp one maroon 3x3 glyph in each corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:37:#          source output = full periodic lattice + centered maroon 2x2 plus\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:39:#                          + four corner maroon plus stamps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:41:#          source output = full periodic lattice + centered maroon 2x2 X\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:43:#                          + four corner maroon X stamps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:57:#    - The original centered 2x2 maroon stamp assumption is invalid now and must be removed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:65:#      If corner stamping happened earlier, the erase pass would delete the maroon markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:88:#    - No extra color mapping is introduced: output colors stay {black, orange, maroon}.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:89:#    - The meaning of maroon is still \"decoded glyph marker\", but its placement changes from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:164:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into a tiled lattice, erase that lattice down to a symmetry-selected aperture, and leave the center as a black hole with maroon corner stamps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:176:    - Stamp one maroon 3x3 copy of the glyph into each of the four output corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:255:    # Outside the kept aperture, only the four corner maroon stamps are allowed to survive.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/10/code.py:16:#    [maroon, yellow, blue, teal], and counts [2, 1, 1, 1]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/10/code.py:18:#    - D4-only output:       [grey, yellow, blue + {maroon, maroon, teal}]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/10/code.py:19:#    - fused output here:    [grey, grey, blue + {maroon, maroon, teal}, grey]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/43/code.py:36:#      original foreground color from the input rather than being recolored to maroon(9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/43/code.py:43:#      maroon center, whereas the combo produces black cross-shaped holes on an orange\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/43/code.py:78:#    - The center also preserves the input color instead of switching to maroon, giving an\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/43/code.py:86:#    - Even when the foreground color is dark (for example blue or maroon is excluded), the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/27/code.py:23:#            maroon sprite -> grey frame\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/25/code.py:16:#    - Output remains a 16x16 black/orange lattice plus the centered 6x6 maroon 2x2 stamp of the original glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/25/code.py:27:#                     and the final partial band also follows the same parity. The maroon center stamp is unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/25/code.py:43:#    - The output size formula and the centered 6x6 maroon stamp remain valid because they depend only on the fixed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/25/code.py:61:#    - The output still has only two layers: background lattice and central maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/25/code.py:67:#    - Output still uses only black, orange, and maroon, so the new reasoning burden is spatial, not chromatic.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/25/code.py:171:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a variable-period alternating lattice, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/25/code.py:182:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true cells to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/26/code.py:17:#     repeat that tile over 16x16, then place a centered 2x2 maroon stamp of the glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/26/code.py:31:#   - Finally, the same observed asymmetric glyph is tiled 2x2 in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/26/code.py:58:#   `np.rot90` after `tile_fill(...)` and before the maroon center stamp is painted.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/26/code.py:71:# - The centered maroon stamp stays in the input orientation, which gives the human solver a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/26/code.py:78:#   maroon overlay. No extra objects or auxiliary markers are introduced.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/26/code.py:79:# - Only three output colors remain in use: black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/26/code.py:83:#   before rotation (ignoring the maroon stamp). It must be positive whenever the sampled\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/26/code.py:206:    - Read the motif's orientation as a whole-canvas `np.rot90` count, rotate the tiled lattice by that amount, then tile the observed oriented motif 2x2 and recolor its true cells to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/45/code.py:30:#     - combining them yields four 3x3 maroon glyph copies at quadrant-like slots:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/45/code.py:37:#     - enlarge the maroon event by tiling the glyph 2x2 into one centered 6x6 block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/45/code.py:43:#     - maroon no longer forms one large central 6x6 object\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/45/code.py:66:#   - maroon overlays only the orange/black lattice, never another maroon stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/45/code.py:69:#   - maroon pixel count is not enough because four 3x3 native stamps can match the original 2x2-tiled stamp count\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/45/code.py:70:#   - a useful anti-degeneration metric is the maroon union bbox:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/45/code.py:129:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour motif into a 16x16 periodic lattice with several small maroon glyph stamps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/45/code.py:139:    - Recolor the original 3x3 glyph to maroon and place one native-size copy at each site of a regular 2x2 slot lattice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/45/code.py:142:    - The input glyph still serves as a phase code for the full orange lattice, but its output copy behavior has changed: it is no longer enlarged into one center block and is instead distributed as several equally spaced 3x3 maroon marks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/45/code.py:193:        maroon_mask = out == Color.MAROON\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/45/code.py:194:        maroon_box = bbox(maroon_mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/45/code.py:195:        assert maroon_box == (1, 1, 14, 14)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/17/code.py:42:       solids = [S1(blue), S2(maroon), S3(teal)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/17/code.py:45:       right top->bottom = [S1(blue), S2(maroon), S3(teal)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/17/code.py:47:       paired color swap -> frames use [blue, maroon, teal], solids use [red, green, yellow]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/17/code.py:48:       left bottom-up placement means top->bottom left becomes [F3(teal), F2(maroon), F1(blue)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/31/code.py:127:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice, then replace one aligned lattice cell with a maroon copy of the glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/31/code.py:137:    - Use the raw 3x3 glyph once, recolor its true pixels to maroon, and snap that 3x3 stamp to the nearest 3x3 tile boundary so it exactly covers one lattice cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/27/code.py:19:#      full anymore; maroon appears only where tiled-glyph pixels also lie on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/27/code.py:23:#      all 20 plus pixels in the centered 6x6 tiled plus become maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/27/code.py:26:#      maroon; the other 12 plus pixels stay as teal/black lattice pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/27/code.py:32:#    - The center AND rule is visible for every glyph: seam-overlap maroon counts\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/27/code.py:37:#      background variation is obvious in the input, reduced maroon is obvious\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/27/code.py:65:#    - In the output, the center maroon is visibly sparser than the base task\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/27/code.py:72:#      background-derived lattice color, and maroon. This keeps the center AND\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/27/code.py:80:#      maroon pattern is always a subset of the tiled glyph, never an unrelated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/27/code.py:87:#      candidate whose center maroon count is empty or equals the full glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/27/code.py:168:    Read a color-coded 3x3 contour glyph from a non-fixed background, expand it into a 16x16 periodic lattice, and show maroon only at center seam/glyph crossings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/27/code.py:178:    - Tile the glyph 2x2 into the centered 6x6 box, but recolor to maroon only where those tiled glyph pixels also lie on the box's 3-step seam rows or seam columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/27/code.py:194:    maroon_mask = center & _lattice_seam_mask(center.shape)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/27/code.py:198:    out[r0 : r0 + center.shape[0], c0 : c0 + center.shape[1]][maroon_mask] = Color.MAROON\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/27/code.py:220:    maroon_count = int((center_box == Color.MAROON).sum())\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/27/code.py:221:    if not (0 < maroon_count < full_glyph_count):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/8/code.py:79:#    - Output colors remain the original black/orange/maroon trio, so the new difficulty\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/8/code.py:225:    Decode a contour glyph from a marker-addressed noisy 3x3 patch, then render the same 16x16 lattice and centered maroon stamp as the base task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/8/code.py:235:    - Decode that recovered glyph into the period-3 orange/black tile, repeat it over the 16x16 output, and stamp a 2x2 maroon tiling of the glyph in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/24/code.py:20:      step3: overwrite the centered coarse 2x2 block with maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/24/code.py:25:      colors: black, orange, maroon only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/24/code.py:31:      final_write: direct 16x16 lattice plus flat 6x6 maroon overwrite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/24/code.py:40:        coarse_center: rows 4..5 and cols 4..5 become maroon macro cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/24/code.py:41:        final_effect: every orange or maroon macro cell becomes a 4x4 plus-shaped child stamp, giving a 40x40 perforated lattice\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/24/code.py:51:    - The design stays learnable because only one recursion level, one centered maroon macro block, and three output colors are used.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/24/code.py:58:    - The maroon mark cannot be painted after expansion as one flat rectangle, because that would erase the fractal holes. It must replace a centered 2x2 block in the coarse raster before recursive expansion.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/24/code.py:59:    - `_expand_by_glyph()` assumes coarse pixels are only black/orange/maroon; `_build_coarse_raster()` enforces exactly that palette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/24/code.py:73:    - The centered maroon feature is still a single contiguous macro region, but it inherits the same glyph perforation as the orange lattice, so the scene stays readable instead of becoming a flat overwrite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/24/code.py:77:    - Output colors stay structurally interpretable: orange for phase-on macro cells, maroon for the centered macro stamp, black for empty macro cells and all holes inside child glyph tiles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/24/code.py:220:    - Tile that phase over a 10x10 coarse raster and overwrite the centered coarse 2x2 block with maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/24/code.py:221:    - Expand each coarse pixel into a size-matched child tile shaped like the same enlarged glyph: orange cells become orange glyph tiles, maroon cells become maroon glyph tiles, and black cells stay all black.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/41/code.py:28:#    Example: if a red lane has 3 maroon sprites and the green lane has 2 blue sprites, the seed output would show\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/41/code.py:29:#    3 grey maroon-lane sprites and 5 blue green-lane sprites. The combo output instead keeps the 3 maroon sprites\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/41/code.py:30:#    intact and adds only 1 new maroon sprite to the green lane, so the destination ends with 2 blue + 1 maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/33/code.py:33:#     - the fused output is therefore a 21x21 orange/black lattice with four 9x9 maroon stamps at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/33/code.py:76:#   - multiple 9x9 maroon regions are obvious in every output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/33/code.py:81:#   - maroon overlays only the orange/black lattice\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/33/code.py:85:#   - output colors stay simple and structural: black/orange lattice plus maroon stamps only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/33/code.py:197:    - Build a 9x9 maroon stamp from a 3x3 arrangement of the glyph, rotating each local 3x3 copy by the fixed turn map.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/33/code.py:201:    - The input glyph still controls the orange lattice phase, but its maroon imprint is no longer one centered plain repetition:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/1/code.py:30:#      phase (0,0), then stamp the 2x2 center copy in maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/1/code.py:32:#      a different offset for another color, while the center remains maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/1/code.py:34:#      recolored according to the glyph color instead of always maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/1/code.py:44:#    black, and at most one case reuses maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/1/code.py:79:#    red(2)   -> phase (1,0), stamp maroon(9)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/1/code.py:81:#    No case matches the exact original behavior (zero shift + maroon stamp), so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/1/code.py:235:    # differ from maroon. With the current tables this is true for every color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/3/code.py:28:#    - Recoloring all center glyph cells to maroon is invalid under D4/0; both layers must retain their original\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/11/code.py:22:#     one centered 12x12 maroon stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/11/code.py:43:#   - maroon overwrite remains safe because only the centered stamp is recolored; the background lattice underneath is irrelevant\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/11/code.py:51:#   - only one compact maroon object is overlaid on the lattice, so the output remains readable despite the larger center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/11/code.py:53:#   - output colors stay {black, orange, maroon}; the fusion only changes shape construction, not palette complexity\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/11/code.py:141:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into the original periodic lattice and place a larger rotation-stitched maroon seal at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/11/code.py:151:    - Enlarge each rotated glyph by turning every pixel into a 2x2 block, stitch the four 6x6 results into a centered 12x12 seal, and recolor its true cells to maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/11/code.py:220:    maroon = out == Color.MAROON\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/11/code.py:221:    maroon_box = bbox(maroon)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/11/code.py:222:    if maroon_box != (2, 2, 13, 13):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/11/code.py:226:    if int(maroon.sum()) <= int(legacy_enlarged.sum()):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/37/code.py:8:# orange/black lattice, then stamp a maroon 2x2 copy at the center\" backbone,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/37/code.py:18:#   - place the 6x6 maroon stamp in the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/37/code.py:27:#   - keep the centered 6x6 maroon 2x2 stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/37/code.py:32:#   - the same contour stamp still appears in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/37/code.py:66:#   maroon stamp always fits with non-negative start indices.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/37/code.py:78:# - The lattice remains a single repeated orange/black texture, and the maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/37/code.py:171:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into an asymmetric rectangular lattice and stamp a maroon 2x2 copy at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/37/code.py:178:      orange, nor maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/37/code.py:187:      the original glyph as a centered 6x6 maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/7/code.py:129:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 rhombic lattice whose two diagonal axes use different periods, then stamp the motif in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/7/code.py:139:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and overwrite its true cells with maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/42/code.py:21:#    same structure with 3-pixel bands. The center 6x6 maroon stamp stays unchanged,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/42/code.py:44:#    The lattice is still a single repeated background pattern plus one maroon center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/42/code.py:141:    - Fill the 16x16 output by tiling this expanded orange/black lattice, then stamp a 2x2 repetition of the input glyph in maroon inside the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/35/code.py:60:#      black/orange/maroon. Input colors only partition candidate objects from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/35/code.py:159:    Extract the repeated 3x3 contour code from a noisy 6x6 orange grid, then render the same 16x16 periodic lattice and central maroon stamp as in the base task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/35/code.py:169:    - Decode that mask into the period-3 orange/black tile, repeat it over the 16x16 canvas, then stamp a 2x2 maroon tiling of the glyph into the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/32/code.py:19:#         maroon 2x2 stamp of the original glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/32/code.py:34:#      7. The 6x6 maroon center stamp is still a 2x2 tiling of the input glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/32/code.py:39:#      the output becomes 11x22 before the centered 6x6 maroon H-stamp is added.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/32/code.py:73:#      maroon stamp. No extra markers are introduced.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/32/code.py:79:#    - Output still uses only black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/32/code.py:142:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a rectangular anisotropic lattice, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the output center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/32/code.py:152:    - Convert the coarse 3x3 phase tile into that rectangular period, tile it across an output whose height and width each use their own period formula, and then place a centered 6x6 maroon 2x2 stamp of the original glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b80bb43/6/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形中心提示\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/17/code.py:14:      2. D4/4 side: the centered 2x2 glyph stamp no longer uses fixed maroon; its color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/17/code.py:25:      - the center 6x6 stamp is maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/17/code.py:56:    - The original fixed center overwrite with maroon is also invalid: the stamp color now\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/17/code.py:82:      single variant: outputs must differ from both the fixed-maroon lattice-transfer case\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/15/code.py:67:#      maroon stamp. The two clues support two distinct inferences.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/15/code.py:212:    Read a palette legend from the top strip and a contour glyph from the 6x6 body's border, then combine both to build the periodic lattice and centered maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/15/code.py:222:    - Tile a 16x16 canvas with the phase using the legend-selected colors, then place a 2x2 maroon tiling of the reconstructed glyph in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/38/code.py:16:#      offset, and centered 6x6 maroon stamp. Only the glyph shape changed the background tile.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/38/code.py:49:#      lattice phase and the maroon stamp together, but by different formulas: modulo-3 for background, scaling for\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/38/code.py:52:#    - Output still uses only black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/38/code.py:130:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a variable-sized periodic lattice whose phase and maroon stamp placement are both controlled by the glyph's input placement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/38/code.py:141:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 into a 6x6 stamp, recolor its true cells to maroon, and place that stamp at a position obtained by scaling the input bbox top-left into the legal output stamp-origin range.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/40/code.py:15:#   Originally that produced an orange/black lattice and a maroon center stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/40/code.py:26:#   \"center glyph pixels are maroon\" are both invalid now and must be replaced with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/40/code.py:43:#   Foreground colors exclude black, orange, and maroon, so the fused output cannot\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/39/code.py:12:#      canvas, and the same 3x3 glyph is tiled 2x2 as a centered 6x6 maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/39/code.py:25:#      denser period-4 lattice behind the centered maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/39/code.py:49:#    - `center = np.tile(motif, (2, 2))` still holds, but now the centered maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/39/code.py:68:#      lattice and one centered maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/39/code.py:188:    Decode the enlarged 4x4 contour glyph into a period-4 orange/black lattice and stamp a 2x2 maroon copy of that glyph at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/39/code.py:198:    - Fill a black 16x16 canvas by repeating that period-4 tile, then tile the original 4x4 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 8x8 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/20/code.py:26:#     - output is still a 16x16 orange/black period-3 lattice with a centered 6x6 maroon overlay\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/20/code.py:53:#         - both the repeated lattice and the maroon center now expose orientation, so a rotated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/20/code.py:79:#     - the maroon center reinforces the rule by displaying a four-quadrant rotation cycle derived\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/20/code.py:82:#     - only black, orange, and maroon appear in the output, preserving the original palette discipline\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/20/code.py:84:#       the maroon overwrite is confined to the central 6x6 square\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/20/code.py:161:    Decode a rotated asymmetric 3x3 glyph into an oriented period-3 lattice, then place a rotating maroon stamp at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/20/code.py:171:    - In the centered 6x6 region, place four maroon copies of the observed motif arranged as a rotation cycle: 0 degrees, clockwise 90, 180, and counterclockwise 90.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:25:#      a centered 6x6 maroon 2x2 stamp of that glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:65:#    - The center overwrite assumes maroon can be painted on top of either lattice color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:79:#      black/orange periodic lattice everywhere, plus a maroon 2x2 stamp only in the centered\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:83:#      for the direct glyph-derived phase cells, and maroon for the center stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:167:    Reinterpret the colored 3x3 contour glyph as a directly copied phase mask, invert the lattice color roles, and stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:177:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 into the centered 6x6 region and recolor the glyph pixels to maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:19:#        2. tile the 3x3 glyph 2x2 into a 6x6 maroon center stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:22:#        2. the maroon glyph is moved to exactly one corner, chosen by glyph type\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:24:#        source: decode plus -> lattice -> 6x6 maroon plus-tiling at rows/cols 5..10\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:26:#                place one 3x3 maroon plus at the top-left corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:45:#    - The fused rule therefore uses a single 3x3 maroon glyph in one corner. This\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:58:#        2. exactly one corner contains the maroon glyph, and which corner it is varies\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:67:#        maroon overwrite only in one 3x3 corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:72:#    - The output uses only black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:149:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice with a black center void and a glyph-specific maroon corner stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:159:    - Overwrite the centered 6x6 area with pure black, then place one maroon 3x3 copy of the glyph into the corner assigned to that glyph class.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:162:    - The input contour now controls two output attributes at once: it still determines the orange lattice phase, and it also selects which corner receives the only maroon glyph while the center stays empty.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:224:    maroon_corners = [name for name, view in corner_views.items() if np.any(view == Color.MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:225:    if maroon_corners != [glyph_name]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/9/code.py:24:#     - output stays a 16x16 orange/black period-3 lattice with a centered 6x6 maroon overlay\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/9/code.py:83:#     - the output still uses only black, orange, and maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/9/code.py:150:    Treat the colored 3x3 asymmetric glyph as an oriented phase code, then render a mirrored maroon stamp at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/9/code.py:161:    - In the centered 6x6 region, place four transformed maroon copies of the glyph: original, horizontal flip, vertical flip, and 180-degree rotation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/32/code.py:10:#    我把可见模式收紧为两类，正好对应题意里的“十字形 vs 单点”：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:24:#     - output stays a 16x16 black/orange period-3 lattice with a centered 6x6 maroon stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:38:#       4. tile the rotated phase across 16x16, then stamp the observed 111/100/100 motif in maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:58:#     - the centered 6x6 maroon stamp is unchanged and safely overwrites the tiled lattice last\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:60:#     - a human sees the oriented glyph twice: once in the input and again as the 2x2 maroon stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:66:#     - only three colors appear in the output: black, orange, maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:167:    - Repeat the rotated phase tile over the 16x16 black canvas, then tile the observed motif 2x2 and recolor its true cells to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/21/code.py:22:#    repeat one orange/black lattice -> stamp that glyph in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/21/code.py:31:#    the earlier one on shared cells. The center stamp stays a single 2x2 maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/21/code.py:59:#    The output still uses only black, two layer colors, and one centered maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/21/code.py:178:    Decode two colored copies of the same contour glyph into shifted lattice layers, then place the shared glyph as a centered maroon seal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/21/code.py:188:    - Composite the two shifted lattices so the later bbox in row-major order overwrites the earlier one on overlap, then stamp the shared glyph tiled 2x2 in maroon inside the centered 6x6 window.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/26/code.py:10:#   2 层或 3 层的嵌套槽，外层只是通道，真正目标是最内层。比如一个向下开口的 3 层结构，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:17:#   output still consists of a tiled orange/black phase lattice plus a centered 2x2 maroon stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:51:#   comfortably larger than the fixed 6x6 maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:57:# - Foreground color is chosen from the same safe set excluding black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:69:#   maroon stamp. No extra markers are added.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:75:#   color, while the output still uses only black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:139:    - Tile the phase tile across that canvas, then place a centered 6x6 maroon stamp made by 2x2 tiling of the original glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/27/code.py:20:#     - Warm-colored movable pieces come in exactly two visibly related shades: red and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/27/code.py:62:#     - The shade cue is purely visual: red versus maroon component counts.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:26:#   - a maroon stamp is always the 2x2 tiling of the 3x3 glyph, so each stamp is 6x6\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:36:#     - output gets one centered 6x6 maroon stamp at (5, 5)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:62:#   - maroon stamps are large and repeated, making the regular spacing easy to see\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:156:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice and stamp a shifted 2x2 maroon stamp array.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:166:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 to form a 6x6 maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:170:    - The glyph carries two independent visible signals: its shape still determines the orange phase lattice, while its input position now controls the global offset of an evenly spaced four-stamp maroon array.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/5/code.py:148:    Decode the 3x3 contour cue into the original 16x16 periodic lattice, then stamp a mixed-symmetry 2x2 arrangement of that glyph in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/5/code.py:158:    - In the centered 6x6 window, place four 3x3 maroon copies of the glyph using a mixed D4 layout:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/28/code.py:27:#   4. Put a centered 6x6 maroon stamp made from a plain 2x2 copy of the input glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/28/code.py:39:#   by one row, and the centered maroon stamp is built from mirrored copies of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/28/code.py:69:# - Inside the center, maroon is the only overlay color and stays confined to one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/28/code.py:184:    Decode one colored 3x3 contour glyph into a color-transferred phase lattice, then place a mirrored maroon stamp at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/28/code.py:195:    - Repeat the colored phase seed over the 16x16 black canvas, then place a centered 6x6 maroon mirror-collage\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D18/2/code.py:3:# Change: 使用预定义的形状库（矩形、L形、T形、十字形等 16 种基础形状），3-6 种被选入每道题... → 随机生成洞形状（非预定义库）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/34/code.py:34:#   the maroon center stamp and the orange/black lattice both rotate together.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/34/code.py:59:#   The output still uses the original three-color palette (black, orange, maroon), so the new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/34/code.py:175:    - Build the same 16x16 orange/black lattice and centered 2x2 maroon stamp as the canonical family would produce, then rotate the entire finished canvas by the recovered quarter-turn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:18:#       color: any single color except black(0), grey(5), orange(7), maroon(9)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:23:#     stamp: the original 4x4 motif tiled 2x2 into a centered 8x8 maroon block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:24:#     colors_used: black(0), grey(5), orange(7), maroon(9)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:75:#    - The centered maroon stamp exposes the exact 4x4 motif geometry, giving the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:87:#      maroon for the stamp. The third lattice color always comes from the same logical\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:196:    Read a 4x4 contour code, expand it into a period-4 tricolor lattice, and stamp a centered maroon 2x2 copy of the motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:206:    - Repeat that 4x4 tricolor tile over a 16x16 canvas, then place a 2x2 maroon tiling of the original motif in the centered 8x8 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:17:#      output is still 16x16 and still ends with a centered 6x6 maroon 2x2 stamp of that glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:22:#      3. The maroon stamp is written last on top.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:38:#      stamps the 6x6 maroon H pattern. The center region therefore has two visible rhythms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:61:#    - Original final maroon overwrite remains valid and must still happen last.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:68:#    - The detail window is fixed to rows/cols 3..12 and the 6x6 maroon stamp sits at rows/cols\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:81:#      overlay, maroon stamp. The two tiled layers share the same orange/black palette and combine\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:90:#      maroon stamp copied from the input glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:226:    Decode one 3x3 contour glyph into a two-scale tiled scene whose background and center detail use different period tables, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:236:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon inside the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:20:#      into a 6x6 maroon stamp -> place that stamp at the fixed centered box\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:24:#      3x3 into a 9x9 maroon stamp -> aim for the geometric center first, then snap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:30:#      snaps that to the nearest period-3 boundary, namely (3,3). The final maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:35:#      lattice decoding. This keeps the task readable while making the maroon region\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:62:#      the intended maroon-over-lattice overwrite already present in the base task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:67:#    - The maroon area becomes both larger and shifted relative to naive centering.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:75:#    - The output still has only three colors: black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:178:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into a periodic 16x16 lattice, then overlay a larger maroon stamp snapped to the lattice grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:188:    - Tile the original glyph 3x3 to build a 9x9 stamp, recolor its True pixels to maroon, and place it at the nearest legal 3x3 tile boundary rather than at the old fixed center box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:191:    - The contour still determines the lattice phase, but the stamp geometry is now governed by two coupled constraints: it is larger because of 3x3 tiling, and it must sit on the lattice's own 3x3 boundary system, so the maroon region lands as a clean 3-by-3 block of tiles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/4/code.py:34:#      bottom band: D=3x3 maroon, E=3x5 yellow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/4/code.py:37:#    global area sequence B(yellow), C(green), D(maroon), A(green), E(yellow).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/4/code.py:42:#      maroon block: D\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:33:#      phase pattern of the decoded glyph. The centered 6x6 maroon 2x2 stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:70:#      maroon center stamp still anchors the correspondence to the input glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:76:#      the maroon center stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:79:#      maroon keeps its center-stamp role, and the input's two non-orange colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:212:    Recover a 3x3 contour glyph from a textured 6x6 board, then render its decoded lattice with thicker black grid lines and the usual centered maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:222:    - Tile that 4x4 carrier across the 16x16 output and place a 2x2 maroon tiling of the recovered glyph in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/2/code.py:20:#     - 同一滑行通道上再放一个更近的错形红诱饵，肉眼能看到“最近的不一定会进入槽里”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/2/code.py:25:#     - 输出时，真匹配块按匹配后的朝向滑入槽内；原始位置和中间通道都变黑；近处错形块与所有其他红块一起被擦除。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/2/code.py:38:#     - 真红块和诱饵都只放在槽口外的背景通道中，不进入结构实体，也不会越界。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/2/code.py:44:#     - 结构之间通常保留 2-3 格缓冲，单个补丁的黑轨迹和红块都局限在一个窄通道内，避免多层覆盖导致难以阅读。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/29/code.py:32:#   让蓝水先占据粗糙台阶和右侧盆地，再把红水放进去。于是红水虽然起点更低，却更晚遇到通道。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/29/code.py:41:# - 几何结构只使用一个很窄的主通道和一个右侧接收盆地，再通过镜像和蓝水高度/宽度的小变化产生样例，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/29/code.py:66:# - 整个场景只保留一个上层导流台、一个下层发射带、一个粗糙肩部和一个右侧接收盆地，避免多通道叠加。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/5/code.py:17:#       本实现采用固定色序 [9, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3]，即 maroon -> orange -> pink -> grey -> yellow -> green。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/41/code.py:63:#    - All three glyph colors are distinct and avoid black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/41/code.py:68:#      repeated lattice color, while its shape reappears as the maroon center stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/41/code.py:73:#      plus one centered maroon stamp, matching the base task's clean composition.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/41/code.py:77:#    - Color usage is constrained to one meaningful transferred color plus maroon on black, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/41/code.py:191:    - Exactly three macro-cells are occupied, and each occupied cell contains one monochrome 3x3 contour glyph in a unique non-black, non-orange, non-maroon color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/41/code.py:197:    - Instruction 3 uses its glyph shape as a rotation code; rotate both the decoded phase tile and the stamp motif by 0, 90, 180, or 270 degrees, then tile the 16x16 canvas and stamp the rotated 6x6 motif in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形标记+两层嵌套恢复\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/6/code.py:18:#       color: any single color except black(0), orange(7), maroon(9)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/6/code.py:24:#     stamp: the original 4x4 motif tiled 2x2 into a centered 8x8 maroon block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/6/code.py:25:#     colors_used: black(0), orange(7), maroon(9)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/6/code.py:47:#        Therefore output = 20x20, and the 8x8 maroon center stamp sits inside a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/6/code.py:80:#      centered maroon stamp. The larger 20x20 canvas actually increases separation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/6/code.py:82:#      maroon block does not introduce awkward off-center clipping.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/6/code.py:86:#    - Output colors remain restricted to black/orange/maroon, so the new rule is about\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/6/code.py:184:    Decode the colored 4x4 contour motif into a tightly tiled 20x20 period-4 lattice and stamp a centered maroon 2x2 copy of that motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/6/code.py:194:    - Tile the original 4x4 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 8x8 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/21/code.py:46:# - 结构之间仍保持 padding；distractor 仍禁止落在任何 socket 向外的清晰视线通道上，因此不会误变成 matched。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/21/code.py:62:# - 规则完全由可见几何关系驱动：是否处在某个结构开口的视线通道上，决定它是“滑入”还是“原地保留”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/30/code.py:23:#    - The generator rejects cases where the fine layer adds too little or adds only under the maroon stamp, preventing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/30/code.py:33:#    - The original center stamp recolored one layer. Here the maroon stamp must use the union of both color layers,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/30/code.py:40:#    - The fine overlay window is fixed to rows/cols 4..11 and the maroon stamp to rows/cols 5..10, so all overlays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/30/code.py:49:#    - Only three output colors are used: black, orange, maroon. The two input colors are not copied through, which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/30/code.py:51:#    - The fine overlay is confined to the centered 8x8 window, and the maroon stamp is drawn last in the smaller 6x6\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/30/code.py:55:#      encoded orange/black tilings plus one maroon union stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/30/code.py:56:#    - The generator enforces positive fine-layer gain outside the maroon stamp, so the second code color always has an\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/30/code.py:238:    Decode a two-color 3x3 code patch into a coarse global lattice plus a finer centered overlay, then stamp the full glyph union in maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/30/code.py:248:    - Decode the fine layer into a 2x2 orange/black tile and repeat it only in the centered 8x8 region, union-overlaid on top of the coarse background; then tile the union of both input layers 2x2 and recolor it to maroon in the centered 6x6 stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/45/code.py:74:# - 生成器还保证至少一部分水离开源高台并进入底盆，否则这两个新增通道都不够明显。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/14/code.py:15:#    - Output still has a 16x16 orange/black lattice plus a maroon 2x2 stamp of the glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/14/code.py:26:#      coarse and highly visible: the whole lattice shifts, and the large maroon stamp moves.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/14/code.py:47:#      solid maroon stamp. No extra markers or hidden encodings are introduced.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/14/code.py:50:#    - No new color mapping is introduced. Orange/black still encode the lattice and maroon still\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/14/code.py:98:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour motif into a 16x16 periodic lattice whose phase and maroon stamp position both depend on the motif's input placement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/14/code.py:109:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2, recolor its True cells to maroon, scale `(r0, c0)` from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/14/code.py:114:      while proportional scaling decides where the maroon stamp lands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/14/code.py:41:#      blue<->red, pink<->orange, teal<->maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/14/code.py:91:    8: 9,  # teal -> maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/14/code.py:92:    9: 8,  # maroon -> teal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/12/code.py:63:#      central maroon 6x6 stamp stays constant while the orange/black lattice\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/12/code.py:69:#      the full canvas and one centered maroon stamp on top.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/12/code.py:72:#      markers only; the output still uses exactly black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/12/code.py:141:    Recover the lone valid 3x3 contour code from a noisy variable-size orange square, then expand it into the corresponding periodic lattice and centered maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/12/code.py:151:    - Tile the recovered 3x3 glyph 2x2 into a 6x6 mask and recolor its true cells to maroon at the exact center of the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/5/code.py:26:#   则是该 2x4 红块移动到结构外侧贴边位置，原位置变回背景，6 格通道保持纯背景，其他干扰红块不动。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/5/code.py:57:#   推理通道里。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/5/code.py:58:# - 没有黑拖尾后，输出更干净；为了防止“终点和原地红块混成一团”，front-ray 约束禁止在终点通道上放置\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/31/code.py:25:#      (label yellow -> swatch maroon)] in that shuffled order\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/42/code.py:50:#    - `_simulate()` 允许多个活动分支，但默认它们不会在狭窄通道内彼此抢占；生成器用分叉后左右分盆来保证。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D8/0/code.py:36:#   使远杯保留 1-3 格后被阻挡。若有第三个杯，则只放在清空通道里，不参与冲突。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:24:    - 原题从目标 3x3 块外的可通行格做普通 BFS，把所有可达 maroon 按步数远近搬回目标块。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:25:      例如某个 maroon 离入口 4 步、另一个 6 步，那么 4 步的先进入目标，即使那条路一直贴着墙走。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:26:    - 融合后仍然只允许沿 orange/maroon 的 4 连通路径到达，但“距离”不再是步数，而是：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:28:    - 具体小例子：一枚 maroon 在入口旁边的 2 格死胡同里，路径两格都被三面墙夹住，总代价可能是\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:29:      3 + 3 = 6；另一枚更远的 maroon 在较宽主通道深处，沿路 5 格每格只贴 1 面墙，总代价只有 5。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:35:    - 迷宫保留单一目标块、单一墙色、单一 token 色；复杂度来自通道几何而不是对象种类膨胀。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:36:    - generator 强制同时出现较宽主通道和狭窄支路，并筛掉“新旧前 k 个来源集合完全相同”的样本，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:41:      保证 reachable 区里确实有不同宽度、不同贴墙程度的通道。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:42:    - 原 main() 只需要至少一个入口；融合后若把所有可达通道都做成等宽直廊，新规则会退化。生成器\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:43:      因此显式做“主通道加宽 + 支路保持狭窄 + 近处死胡同”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:44:    - 原 main() 依赖“可达 maroon 数 = 要填入目标的数量”。这一点仍保留，所以生成器只放 k 个可达\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:45:      maroon，其余 maroon 全都放在隔离口袋里做 distractor。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:47:    - 目标块固定在 11x11 的中心 3x3；除目标块外，其余单元只会是 floor、wall 或 maroon。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:48:    - 迷宫从单个入口接到外部主通道，支路和加宽单元都只在非目标区域内生成，不越界、不覆盖目标块。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:51:    - 人类可以直接看到：有些 maroon 虽然步数更近，但卡在三面贴墙的死胡同；另一些更远，却位于\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:52:      较宽或半开阔的主通道里。输出若优先搬走后者，说明排序标准不是普通 BFS。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:53:    - 由于目标块仍按 row-major 填入，观察者只需比较“哪些 maroon 消失了”，就能对照迷宫几何推断\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:56:    - 场景仍只有五种颜色，且各自语义稳定：orange 地板、magenta 墙、green/red 目标、maroon token。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:61:      作为墙，并构造让这种“贴墙程度”可肉眼比较的通道。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:423:    Move the reachable maroon pixels with the smallest wall-contact path cost into the centered 3x3 target block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:427:    - Orange cells are walkable floor, magenta cells are maze walls, and maroon cells sit on floor cells inside the maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:430:    - Start from every floor/maroon cell directly adjacent to the destination block and traverse only floor or maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:432:    - Keep only reachable maroon pixels, rank them by this accumulated wall-neighbor cost, and place the closest ones into the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:433:    - Any maroon that moves is erased from its source cell and replaced by orange floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:435:    Key insight: In the maze, the winning maroons are not always the fewest steps away; wider passages can beat shorter but tighter dead ends because distance is driven by repeated contact with nearby walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:454:    maroons = [(int(expo[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:455:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:456:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:459:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:460:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/24/code.py:3:# Name: 颜色通道轮换 + 链式传递 + 三组结构\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:15:#      sorts reachable maroons by flood-fill distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:19:#    - Sorting is intentionally decoupled from that path wave: once maroons are known to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:28:#      maroons; otherwise \"sorting\" would be invisible because every reachable token would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:38:#    - Erasing moved maroons back to floor=7 remains valid because the spec keeps the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:41:#    - Walls, destination, source maroons, and sealed distractor pockets are placed on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:47:#    - The output retains some outside maroons because only nine move; this exposes which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:126:def _reachable_maroons(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:129:    maroons: list[tuple[int, int, int]] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:132:            maroons.append((_euclid2(int(r), int(c), cr, cc), int(r), int(c)))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:133:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:134:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:152:    Pull the Euclidean-closest reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:155:    - Orange floor holds scattered maroon tokens, magenta wall cells, and one fixed 3x3 target block whose center is the unique red pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:159:    - Start from every floor/maroon cell that touches the target block in 8-neighbor sense, then flood-fill through floor+maroon with 8-connectivity; this is the reachability test and its path metric is Chebyshev-style 8-step BFS.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:160:    - Keep only maroon pixels reached by that wave, but rank them by Euclidean distance to the red center rather than by flood-fill distance; ties break by row then column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:161:    - Move the best k=min(9, reachable_count) maroons into the destination block in row-major order and erase those source cells back to orange floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:177:    ranked = _reachable_maroons(grid, dist8, cr, cc)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/11/code.py:26:#    - Example: if a cell contains a maroon L-shape on teal and it is queried,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/11/code.py:28:#      the teal border and turns the maroon L-shape into a gray L-shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:9:#      scattered maroon tokens outside the block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:11:#      ranked reachable maroons by increasing BFS distance, and wrote them into\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:14:#      1. Candidate maroons are ranked from far to near.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:26:#      added. With identical maroon tokens, D3 only changes the output when more\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:42:#    - The old `k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))` also breaks because the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:45:#      set should be erased; the extra near maroons must survive in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:50:#    - Source and distractor maroons are sampled only from floor cells outside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:57:#      effects co-occur: far maroons disappear while near ones remain, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:70:#      maroon moves, floor is restored, green stays as empty target cells, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:199:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:200:    maroons = [triple for triple in maroons if triple[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:201:    return dest_cells, fill_order, center, floor, maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:206:    Move the farthest reachable maroon pixels into the destination block while leaving the red center untouched.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:209:    - The board is an orange floor with optional magenta wall barriers and scattered maroon source pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:213:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells touching the target, walking only through floor or maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:214:    - Reachable maroon pixels are ranked from farthest to nearest by BFS distance, with row/column tie-breaks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:215:    - The chosen maroons are erased from their source positions and copied into the target in reverse row-major order starting from the lower-right, but the red center cell is always skipped.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:223:    dest_cells, fill_order, _center, floor, maroons = _analyze_grid(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:225:    maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:226:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:227:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:444:    dest_cells, fill_order, center, floor, maroons = _analyze_grid(inp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:445:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:446:    ordered_far = sorted(maroons, key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:447:    ordered_near = sorted(maroons)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:471:        \"reachable_count\": len(maroons),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:7:#   A canonical corridor sits beside the 3x3 destination block. The first maroon is within\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:9:#   them, and the fourth remains at distance 4 even after earlier maroons disappear. This\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:15:#   In the base task maroon cells were globally passable, so deleting one could not shorten any\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:16:#   route. Here only orange floor is traversable; a maroon may be used only as the final target\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:23:#   Walls isolate one narrow chamber, so a human can see the front maroon disappear first,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:24:#   then notice that deeper maroons become newly available one by one. The untouched fourth\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:25:#   maroon demonstrates the path-length threshold.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:28:#   1. at least one maroon is collected by the fused solver,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:29:#   2. at least two collected maroons were not initially eligible under the threshold,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:30:#   3. an iterative solver without the threshold would collect strictly more maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:289:    Pull maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the unique red center, one shortest-path step at a time.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:297:    - Repeatedly recompute which maroon pixel is reachable from the destination through orange floor cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:298:    - A maroon qualifies only if its current shortest path length is at most 3, where the last step may enter the maroon but other maroons are not traversable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:299:    - On each iteration, move only the single nearest qualifying maroon into the next destination cell in row-major order, erase its source to floor, then recompute from the updated grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:300:    - Stop when the block is full or no maroon remains within the path-length limit.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:303:    - Removing one maroon can open a shorter route to deeper maroons, so the reachable set is dynamic; however the 3-step cap still prevents some connected maroons from ever being collected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/43/code.py:174:    - A magenta rectangular frame surrounds that block; some non-corner frame cells are replaced by maroon markers, and some frame cells are removed as 1-pixel openings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/43/code.py:178:    - A maroon frame marker is collectible only if the flood can touch it from the outside of the rectangle through one of the frame openings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/17/code.py:26:#   original task: a maroon table glyph and its rotated query copy do not match\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/7/code.py:37:#       红色像素，就长出十字形正交射线。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:15:#   In the original task, if six reachable maroon tokens are ranked closest first,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:18:#   so a cropped view of the old output would contain a maroon center once k >= 5.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:36:#   destination block and that at least one adjacent floor/maroon cell exists to seed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:41:#   Source maroons are sampled only from reachable floor cells outside the 3x3 block;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:47:#   maroons around it, making the \"skip center\" rule visible in 2-4 examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:49:#   The cropped output contains only green, red, and maroon inside one 3x3 block, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:94:def _rank_reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:146:    ranked = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:155:    - The full 11x11 scene still contains orange floor, optional magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and one green 3x3 target block around a unique red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:159:    - Flood-fill from passable cells adjacent to the target through orange and maroon cells, ignoring magenta walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:160:    - Sort reachable maroon tokens by BFS distance, then by row and column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:164:    Key insight: The outside world is still needed to decide how many maroons qualify, but the returned grid is only the cropped destination state, with the center acting as a fixed reference point.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:167:    ranked = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:18:#    - The original task does one static BFS, sorts every reachable maroon once, then fills the 3x3 target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:19:#    - This combo turns the wall into a local crumble mechanic: when a maroon is collected, every magenta wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:23:#         2. Take only the currently nearest reachable maroon layer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:29:#    - Only two dynamic gates are used, but each sample contains multiple layers and 5-8 collected maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:31:#    - The layout varies by optional filler maroons and grid rotation/flip, which keeps samples from looking cloned\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:36:#    - A collected maroon may alter the obstacle map, so the solver must mutate a working copy of the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:37:#    - The generator must keep trigger maroons near only their intended gates; otherwise 3x3 crumble would open\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:52:#    - The total collectible maroons stay within 9, so every moved maroon has a destination cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:53:#    - Trigger maroons are spaced so that their 3x3 crumble neighborhoods do not accidentally merge unrelated gates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:77:    \"\"\"Distance from the destination-adjacent frontier through floor/maroon cells; adjacent cells start at 1.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:107:    - final_work: grid after maroons are erased and dynamic walls have crumbled\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:108:    - collected: maroons collected in layer order, row-major inside each layer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:165:def _static_reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:166:    \"\"\"Reachable maroons under the original static-wall interpretation, used only for generator validation/metrics.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:168:    maroons = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON) if (r, c) not in DEST_SET and dist[r, c] > 0]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:169:    maroons.sort(key=lambda rc: (int(dist[rc[0], rc[1]]), rc[0], rc[1]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:170:    return maroons[:DEST_LIMIT]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:175:    Move maroons into the target block by repeatedly taking the current BFS-nearest layer and crumbling nearby walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:178:    - The grid is 11x11 with an orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and a fixed 3x3 green target\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:180:    - Some maroons sit in rooms that are initially sealed by magenta barriers, while earlier reachable maroons sit next\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:184:    - Run BFS from floor/maroon cells adjacent to the target, but collect only the nearest reachable maroon layer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:185:    - After collecting that layer, erase those maroons to floor and turn every wall in each collected maroon's 3x3\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:187:    - Continue until no more maroons are reachable; place the collected maroons into the target block in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:252:    # Hall / room floors remain orange by default. Mark fixed and optional maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:279:    static_reachable = _static_reachable_maroons(inp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/45/code.py:16:#    - The original task sorted every reachable maroon token individually by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/45/code.py:27:#      distance 1: [(6,5,maroon)] -> output cell maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/45/code.py:29:#      The destination begins [grey, maroon, blue, ...] in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/45/code.py:34:#      maroon}. Each sample uses only 2-3 of them, so mixed layers are visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:33:#    - 原来的 `maroons.sort()` 默认是 `(flood_distance,row,col)`; 融合后必须改成\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:36:#    - 原 solver 里“k = min(9, reachable_maroon_count)”仍成立; 新 generator 明确围绕这个容量上限造样例。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:145:def _reachable_maroons(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:151:    maroons = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:155:            maroons.append((rr, cc))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:156:    return maroons, dist\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:181:    maroons, dist = _reachable_maroons(grid, center)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:183:        source_order = _sort_sources_combo(maroons, center)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:185:        source_order = _sort_sources_legacy(maroons, dist)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:212:    maroons, dist = _reachable_maroons(grid, center)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:213:    combo_sources = _sort_sources_combo(maroons, center)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:214:    legacy_sources = _sort_sources_legacy(maroons, dist)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:215:    k = min(9, len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:226:        \"reachable\": len(maroons),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:236:    Pull reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the unique red center,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:240:    - The board is an 11x11 orange floor with optional magenta walls and scattered maroon tokens.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:244:    - First flood-fill outward from floor cells touching the target block, moving only through floor or maroon cells,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:245:      and keep only maroon tokens that are reachable through that passable region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:246:    - Sort the reachable maroon tokens by Euclidean distance to the red center, nearest first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:252:    - Walls still matter, because they decide which maroon tokens are even eligible, but once eligibility is fixed,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/2/code.py:19:#           (teal, orange) -> (yellow, maroon)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/2/code.py:23:#       swap target pairs across shape families: A receives B's legend target (yellow, maroon), and B\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/24/code.py:19:   the hub's top edge is maroon, yellow still goes to the top because row order, not color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:29:      - colors stay orange floor(7), magenta frame/wall(6), green destination ring(3), red center(2), maroon tokens(9)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:30:      - movement is still based on 4-connected flood-fill through floor/maroon cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:31:      - each destination block still fills in row-major order with the closest assigned maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:34:      - maroons are assigned many:many: each token is claimed by the nearest reachable container\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:49:      - each container gets at least one selected maroon from a region that is strictly nearer to that container\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:50:      - at least one selected maroon comes from an overlap region reachable from both containers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:51:      - optional distractor maroons may appear inside the detached frame, unreachable from both containers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:57:      - globally rank reachable maroons and pour them into one container\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:61:      - for each maroon, compare both distance maps and assign the token to the nearer block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:62:      - each block independently sorts its own assigned maroons and fills its own cells in row-major order\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:64:      - with centers at (1,1) and (9,9), a maroon near the upper-left corridor belongs only to the first block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:65:      - a maroon near the lower-right corridor belongs only to the second block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:66:      - a maroon near the middle lanes around the detached frame can be reached from both, so ownership must be decided before filling\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:84:    - original global `maroons[:k]` selection is invalid because each container has its own quota and ownership list\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:91:      - source maroons are sampled only from floor cells outside blocks and outside the frame boundary\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:99:      - every accepted sample has maroons owned by both containers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:100:      - every accepted sample includes at least one overlap maroon reachable from both containers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:108:    - forcing one private maroon per container plus one contested maroon keeps the rule readable from a few examples\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:223:    overlap_maroons = 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:224:    strict_owner_maroons = [0 for _ in containers]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:233:            overlap_maroons += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:238:                strict_owner_maroons[owner] += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:249:        \"overlap_maroons\": overlap_maroons,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:250:        \"strict0\": strict_owner_maroons[0] if strict_owner_maroons else 0,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:251:        \"strict1\": strict_owner_maroons[1] if len(strict_owner_maroons) > 1 else 0,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:258:    Pull maroon pixels into two separated 3x3 containers, each centered on a red marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:261:    - The background is orange floor with scattered maroon source pixels and a detached magenta frame in the middle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:265:    - For each destination block, run a flood-fill distance search through floor/maroon cells, with magenta cells acting as blockers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:266:    - Each reachable maroon is assigned to the nearest block; equal distances are broken by the row-major order of the red centers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:267:    - Within each block, its assigned maroons are sorted by distance then row-major position, erased from their source cells, and written into that block in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:271:    - You must combine two BFS maps with an ownership step: first decide which block owns each maroon, then fill the two containers independently.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:290:    owned_maroons = [[] for _ in containers]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:296:        owned_maroons[owner].append((int(dists[owner][r, c]), r, c))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:299:        owned_maroons[idx].sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:300:        chosen = owned_maroons[idx][: len(dest_cells)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:446:    if features[\"overlap_maroons\"] < 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:20:# - D13/0 is enforced by generation: the number of reachable maroon sources is exactly k, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:28:#   distractor maroons remain to preserve the original flood-fill reachability cue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:55:def _reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, dest_cells: list[tuple[int, int]], dest_set: set[tuple[int, int]], floor: int) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:82:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9) if int(dist[r, c]) < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:83:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:84:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:93:    Move every reachable maroon source into the row-major prefix of a marked 3x3 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:96:    - bg = orange floor, optional magenta walls, scattered maroon (9) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:101:    - Flood-fill from cells adjacent to the destination through floor/maroon cells to find reachable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:102:      maroon sources.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:105:    - Erase the collected source maroons back to floor. On valid instances, the reachable maroon count\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:108:    Key insight: The red pixel no longer just locates the block; it encodes how many reachable maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:109:    should be collected. Walls still matter because only flood-fill-reachable maroons participate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:117:    reachable = _reachable_maroons(grid, dest_cells, dest_set, floor)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/25/code.py:31:    - 原题/阻挡逻辑里：A 的 BR 会先占住通道，B 的 TL 在第一批已画像素处就停止，C 也只会被更早像素截断\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/25/code.py:32:    - 本融合里：A 先向 SE 画完整条通道；随后 B 的 TL 从反方向沿同一组对角线往 NW 走，不会被 A 挡住，而是把共享区段改成 B 的颜色；再之后 C 会把它与 B 共用的那部分再改成 C 的颜色\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:18:#    - Change 1 (D5/1): source tokens can use several visible colors instead of only maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:21:#      blue -> yellow -> teal -> maroon, and within each color group they are sorted by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:25:#      [(d=0, blue), (d=1, maroon), (d=2, yellow), (d=3, blue)].\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:26:#      Original task / D5-only variant would place colors [blue, maroon, yellow, blue].\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:27:#      This combo places [blue, blue, yellow, maroon] because both blue tokens must be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:28:#      consumed before any yellow, and yellow before maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:30:#    - Restrict token colors to a compact palette {blue=1, yellow=4, teal=8, maroon=9}.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:40:#    - `maroons.sort()` was enough before. Now the key must be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:196:    - Collect every reachable token, sort them first by the fixed visible color-group order blue -> yellow -> teal -> maroon, then within each color by flood-fill distance and row/column, and place the chosen colors into the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/34/code.py:32:#       - suppose slot 0 of the query band contains a maroon shape copied from table cell (2, 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/34/code.py:35:#         maroon glyph, and turns the 16 perimeter pixels of that 5x5 cell maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/38/code.py:85:#   \"maroon < teal\" numerically; the secondary key is purely spatial.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:17:#   Original task: reachable maroon pixels were moved into the 3x3 target block, so the chosen\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:18:#   source cells turned back into orange floor; unreachable maroons stayed where they were.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:19:#   This combo changes both ends at once: chosen reachable maroons are copied into the target\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:20:#   block but remain maroon at their original positions, while unreachable maroons are erased.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:21:#   Example sketch: if two reachable maroons and one walled-off maroon are present, the original\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:22:#   output would keep only two maroons inside the block plus the unreachable distractor; the new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:23:#   output keeps the two reachable maroons in place, adds two maroons inside the block, and removes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:27:#   maroons stay in place and the destination uses a single color. To avoid hidden/unobservable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:28:#   degrees of freedom, the generator only creates 2..9 reachable maroons, so every reachable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:29:#   maroon is copied and none are silently excluded by the ranking step. It also forces at least\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:33:#   walls=6, floor=7, maroons=9. It also assumes one red center, a 3x3 target around it, at least\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:34:#   one passable opening adjacent to the block, and maroons placed only on floor cells outside the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:37:#   Walls are painted only outside the destination block; maroons are sampled only from floor cells,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:40:#   copies, reachable corridors keep their maroons, and blocked regions become clean floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:42:#   Across a few examples, a solver can see a stable contrast: maroons connected to a corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:43:#   opening appear twice in the output, while maroons behind walls disappear. No hidden color-value\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:98:def _reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[list[tuple[int, int, int]], np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:126:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:127:    reachable = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:134:    Copy reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the unique red center, while erasing blocked ones.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:137:    - Orange floor carries scattered maroon pixels, and magenta walls may carve the floor into connected and sealed-off regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:141:    - Flood-fill outward from floor or maroon cells touching the destination block, traversing only orange floor and maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:143:    - Those reachable sources stay maroon in place, but any maroon pixel not reached by the flood-fill is erased to orange floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:146:    - The output separates maroons by connectivity, not by raw proximity: corridor-connected maroons survive and also appear inside the block, while wall-isolated maroons disappear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:158:    reachable, _dist = _reachable_maroons(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:160:    all_maroons = {(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:161:    unreachable = all_maroons - reachable_set\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/51/code.py:53:# - 输出里总会有至少 1 格水没有沉到最低盆地，而是停在更高的台面/通道；与“如果继续多轮它还会下去”\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/37/code.py:28:#    grey/orange/maroon. The output paints only blue/green/yellow hub sides; the red hub\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/5/code.py:3:# Name: 颜色通道轮换 + 三组三向交换\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/5/code.py:9:#    - 这个融合版把“类”改成 3 个颜色相位组：同一结构模板上有 3 个变量通道角色，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/5/code.py:18:#      “三相位分组识别 + 沿相位环 A->B->C->A 推进一步”，这一步恰好等价于通道轮换\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/13/code.py:38:#   table has a maroon asymmetric \"hook\" and another maroon different shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/13/code.py:40:#   original task: no cell matches exactly, so neither maroon cell is selected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/13/code.py:41:#   fused task: both maroon cells become yellow in round 1, then only the rotated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/13/code.py:42:#   equivalent hook becomes green in round 2, leaving the other maroon cell yellow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:8:#    - 原题会把 `floor+maroon` 都当作 BFS 通道，所以一条走廊里的整串栗色会一次性全部变成候选，再按距离从近到远选前 k 个。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:16:#    - 原 solver 的 `passable={floor,9}` 在本题已失效；现在栗色必须从通道集合里移除，否则不会产生“前一个栗色挡住后一个”的现象。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:18:#    - 原先把 maroon 自己的 BFS 距离直接读出 `dist[r,c]` 不再成立，因为 maroon 不在 BFS 图里；现在距离改为“相邻已达地板的最短距离 + 1”，并额外兼容直接贴住目标块的栗色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:34:#    - main() 依赖“被收集的栗色底下应当是 floor”；generator 通过先雕 floor 再覆盖 maroon 来保证这一点。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:138:def _reachable_frontier_maroons(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:168:    maroons = [(d, r, c) for (r, c), d in best.items()]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:169:    maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:170:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:182:    initial_frontier = _reachable_frontier_maroons(work, dest_cells, dest_set, floor)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:185:        frontier = _reachable_frontier_maroons(work, dest_cells, dest_set, floor)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:229:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:230:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:231:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:233:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:234:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:244:    Iteratively move the farthest currently exposed maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the lone red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:247:    - Orange cells are the only traversable background; green/red destination cells, magenta walls, and maroon source pixels all behave as solid obstacles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:248:    - A unique red cell marks the middle of a green 3x3 destination block, while maroon pixels sit on narrow floor corridors or in isolated pockets outside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:252:    - At each step, any maroon touching the reached floor region is collectible; choose the farthest such maroon (ties: row, then column), erase it back to floor, and recompute reachability.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:253:    - Stop when the 3x3 block has taken 9 maroons or when no maroon is currently reachable, then write the collected maroons into the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:256:    - Because maroon pixels now block the flood-fill instead of extending it, a removed maroon can reveal new maroons behind it; the final survivors therefore depend on both the iterative unlocking process and the reversed distance preference.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:20:#    (4..6,7), (7,4..6), a maroon at (2,2) is unreachable in the original rule because\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:36:#    - Sorting only matters if more than 9 reachable maroons exist; the generator now\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:37:#      always places exactly 10 reachable maroons and rejects samples where Chebyshev and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:45:#    diagonally positioned maroons, which directly exposes the 8-connectivity change.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:46:#    Because only 9 of 10 maroons move, the leftover source position reveals the distance\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:50:#    wall ring, diagonal openings, and maroon pool stay visually separate, so the input\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:56:#    diagonal corner cells to remain floor or maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:139:def _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, dist):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:141:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:142:    maroons = [triple for triple in maroons if triple[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:143:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:144:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:167:    ranked = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, dist)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:181:    Pull the reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block centered on the unique red cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:185:    - Magenta walls can seal the destination orthogonally while maroon source pixels sit on floor cells outside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:188:    - Start from every passable cell that touches the destination in the 8-neighborhood, then flood-fill through floor/maroon cells using 8-connectivity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:189:    - Rank reachable maroon pixels by the resulting 8-direction shortest-path distance (Chebyshev-style), breaking ties by row then column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:190:    - Move the closest ranked maroons into the destination in row-major order and erase their original positions back to floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:203:    return _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, dist)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:209:    return _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, dist)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/11/code.py:39:      本来会走过但最终保持背景的通道，从而避免逻辑退化和视觉遮挡。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/11/code.py:55:    - solver 新增假设：inactive 边外侧若按原题发射，本应能走出一段背景通道；generator 为其保留完整空走廊，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:3:# Name: 墙壁有通道口+规则矩形框架\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:14:#    The original task already moves reachable maroon tokens into the 3x3 destination by BFS distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:19:#    but do not reach the outside ring where most source maroons live.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:35:#    Humans can compare 2-4 examples and spot the rule because the only moving parts are maroon tokens and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:47:#    - At least one full tunnel reaches the exterior, so reachable maroons can always be placed outside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:48:#    - Distractor pockets are sealed by construction, so unreachable maroons remain unreachable even after\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:120:def _sorted_reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, dist: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:121:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:122:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:123:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:124:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:129:    Pull the reachable maroon tokens through the true frame openings into the 3x3 target block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:138:    - Start a flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination block and move through orange or maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:139:    - Only maroon tokens in the same 4-connected component as a real doorway sequence are candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:140:    - Sort reachable maroons by BFS distance, then by row and column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:141:    - Replace the chosen source cells with orange floor and write the chosen maroons into the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:145:      near the green block is not enough; the path must cross both frames to access the outside maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:158:    maroons = _sorted_reachable_maroons(grid, dist)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:160:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:161:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:272:    maroons = _sorted_reachable_maroons(inp, dist)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:273:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:274:    for _, r, c in maroons[:k]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/30/code.py:27:#      maroon accents near the bottom. Copy the later zigzag into the query band.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:15:#   decision in the output. Example: if three maroon tokens can be reached from the 3x3 target\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:16:#   block and two are trapped behind magenta walls, then the output shows three maroons inside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:22:#   Every generated example contains all three cues simultaneously: destination maroons,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:27:#   maroon=9, trace=5, unreachable=1. The solver still only reads original input colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:29:#   maroons only on floor cells outside that block, and adds a separate sealed 4x4 wall pocket in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:30:#   one corner so at least one unreachable maroon can always be placed without overlap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:36:#   capacity, so every reachable maroon is one of the collected tokens. That avoids leftover\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:37:#   reachable maroons outside the block and keeps the output limited to the intended three cues.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:92:    assert q, \"there must be at least one floor or maroon cell adjacent to the destination block\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:106:    Classify maroon tokens by reachability, move the reachable ones into the center block, and leave visible evidence behind.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:110:    - Green cells form the rest of that destination block, magenta cells act as walls, and maroon cells are scattered tokens on the floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:113:    - Flood-fill outward from floor-or-maroon cells touching the destination block, stopping at magenta walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:114:    - Sort reachable maroon cells by BFS distance, then by row and column; place them into the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:115:    - Each reachable maroon leaves a gray trace at its source position, while each unreachable maroon is recolored blue and stays in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:118:    - The output reveals the full connectivity judgment: maroon inside the block shows which tokens were chosen, gray shows which outside tokens were reachable, and blue shows which ones walls cut off.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:131:    maroons = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:132:    reachable = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in maroons if int(dist[r, c]) < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:133:    unreachable = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in maroons if int(dist[r, c]) >= 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/37/code.py:16:#    - Replace the original \"many scattered maroons -> one center block\" layout with one shared\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/15/code.py:59:  - 只强制单通道覆盖，减少同一区域多层交叉\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:11:#     source_selection: unchanged flood-fill reachability through floor/maroon via 4-neighbors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:17:#       old: the red center could be overwritten if enough maroons were moved\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:34:#       moved: only the closest 8 maroons enter the outer ring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:35:#       preserved: the red center stays red and 2 farther reachable maroons remain outside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:37:#       the partial frontier bends around the perimeter, and saturated cases show a full maroon ring with a red hole\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:43:#       - 4..7 reachable maroons so the spiral prefix is visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:44:#       - 9..11 reachable maroons so skipping the center differs from the pure spiral variant that would fill it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:53:#       - output construction must preserve color 2 at (cr,cc) even when more than 8 reachable maroons exist\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:56:#       - dense-mode examples have at least 9 reachable maroons so the center-skip behavior is exercised\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:58:#     - source maroons are placed only on reachable floor cells, never in the destination or on walls\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:59:#     - extra reachable maroons in dense mode are chosen outside the first 8 ranked cells, so the solver deterministically leaves them behind\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:60:#     - distractor maroons are placed only on unreachable floor cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:169:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center, tracing a spiral that leaves the center untouched.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:172:    - Orange floor cells contain scattered maroon tokens, while magenta walls may block some corridors near the target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:176:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination through floor/maroon cells; only reachable maroons are movable candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:181:    - Two constraints interact: connectivity still decides which maroons qualify, but the destination now behaves like a spiral track wrapped around a permanent red hole.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:200:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:201:    maroons = [triple for triple in maroons if triple[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:202:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:204:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:205:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:37:#     - 原 solver 允许栗色充当 BFS 通道；在本题里栗色恰恰必须终止视线，否则会退化成“同一射线整串都可见”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:125:def _bfs_ranked_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, cr: int, cc: int) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:152:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON) if dist[r, c] >= 0]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:153:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:154:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:163:    ranked = _bfs_ranked_maroons(out, cr, cc)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:240:    Pull the closest straight-line visible maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:248:    - A ray crosses only orange floor and stops at its first non-floor cell; that cell is a candidate only if it is maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:252:    - Being in the same room is no longer enough. The magenta frame puts the block in a corner-biased viewing position, so many maroon pixels are flood-fill reachable but still ignored because no straight ray sees them first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:386:    total_maroons = int((inp == MAROON).sum())\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:387:    if total_maroons < TOTAL_MAROON_RANGE[0] or total_maroons > TOTAL_MAROON_RANGE[1]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:396:    bfs_ranked = _bfs_ranked_maroons(inp, cr, cc)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:397:    bfs_only_maroons = {(r, c) for _, r, c in bfs_ranked} - visible_cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:398:    if not bfs_only_maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/29/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形补丁+交替中心色+凹痕沿直线排列\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/29/code.py:16:#     Odd-index dents get a teal center; even-index dents get a maroon center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/29/code.py:25:#         center -> teal for dent #1, maroon for dent #2, teal for dent #3, ...\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/29/code.py:48:#   - `_main_colors` must not treat maroon as a possible region color in generated inputs, otherwise\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/29/code.py:50:#     teal and maroon from the foreground palette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/29/code.py:61:#       2. at least one even-index dent exists, so maroon appears and the D2 alternation is visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/29/code.py:231:      centers to maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/29/code.py:468:    maroon_count = len(centers) // 2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/29/code.py:469:    if maroon_count < MIN_MAROON_CENTERS:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:31:#   - One maroon trigger sits in the first annulus and one in the second annulus. Collecting the first trigger\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:33:#     segment from the outer frame. Additional maroons wait outside the outer frame and are only collectible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:36:#   - Original task: run one static BFS, keep all reachable maroons, sort once, then fill the destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:42:#       5. Re-run BFS again. The outer-border maroons are now reachable and are collected layer by layer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:44:#       * more maroons move into the 3x3 block;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:52:#   - The first two annuli each contain exactly one trigger maroon. This prevents the dynamic process from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:59:#       * compute reachable maroons,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:66:#       * total collectible maroons never exceeds the 9 destination cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:72:#   - Unreachable distractors are placed in the opposite sealed corridors. They stay visibly maroon in the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:79:#       * later collected maroons line up beyond the newly opened gates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:398:    Pull maroon pixels into the 3x3 block, but only after they unlock nested wall gates layer by layer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:406:    - Run BFS from passable cells adjacent to the destination through floor and maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:407:    - Collect only the nearest BFS layer of reachable maroons at a time. After the first-annulus layer is collected, a short middle-frame gate disappears; after the second-annulus layer is collected, a short outer-frame gate disappears.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:408:    - Recompute BFS after each wall change, continue layer by layer, erase every moved source to floor, and fill the destination cells in row-major order with the collected maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:410:    Key insight: Reachability is no longer static. The nested frames define a staged escape path, and the visible wall removals prove that later maroons are not initially reachable; they become collectible only because earlier BFS layers crack open the next shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:422:    maroons = [\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:427:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:428:    chosen = maroons[: len(DEST_CELLS)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/18/code.py:24:#    the host-region edge are teal; deeper cells are maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/18/code.py:26:#    The center-color rule is intentionally binary (teal vs maroon) rather than using\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/18/code.py:352:      layers of the host-region edge, maroon (9) if it lies deeper inside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:29:#      orange floor, optional magenta walls, and scattered maroon source pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:30:#    - Reachability is unchanged: only maroons connected to the destination through floor/maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:36:#      smaller flood-fill distance, and if a row still contains several maroons at the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:38:#    - Example trace for reachable maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:46:#    - If reachable maroons are <= 9, all of them move and ranking becomes invisible. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:47:#      generator therefore uses 10-14 reachable sources so some maroons remain behind.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:55:#      non-maroon non-destination ring cell. The generator reserves one adjacent floor cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:56:#    - BFS through {floor, maroon} still defines eligibility. What changes is only ranking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:57:#    - The original `maroons.sort()` encoded (distance,row,col). In the combo, ranking must become\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:60:#    - Source maroons are sampled only from reachable floor cells outside the destination block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:68:#    - With >9 reachable maroons, the output exposes the rule through which maroons remain behind.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:69:#      In particular, some earlier-in-column maroons on the same row stay put because a nearer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:70:#      maroon later in that row is selected first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:75:#      maroons move versus remain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:78:#      rows containing multiple reachable maroons require a second observation: closer-in-corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:79:#      maroons win within that row, and equal-distance ties within the row read left-to-right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:94:#    - `_rank_key(..., \"fused\")` assumes distance values are defined for every candidate maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:209:    maroons = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:213:            maroons.append((int(r), int(c), d))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:214:    maroons.sort(key=lambda t: _rank_key(t[0], t[1], t[2], mode))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:216:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:217:    chosen = {(r, c) for r, c, _d in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:228:    Move reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 destination around the red center, using a row-first fused ranking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:231:    - The grid is always 11x11 with a fixed green 3x3 target around one red center, orange floor, optional magenta walls, and maroon pixels scattered on floor cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:232:    - Some maroons are flood-fill reachable from the target through floor/maroon corridors; others may be sealed off behind walls as distractors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:235:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells adjacent to the target, traversing only floor or maroon cells, and keep only reachable maroons as candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:237:    - Move up to nine ranked maroons into the destination in destination row-major order, and clear their source cells back to floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:23:#    - Original rule: a reachable maroon near one corridor gap is moved into the 3x3 target and its old\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:24:#      cell turns back into orange; an unreachable maroon behind a wall stays maroon; the whole 11x11 grid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:26:#    - Fused rule: that same reachable maroon still moves into the target, but its source cell becomes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:27:#      gray(5) to mark \"collected\". A blocked maroon in a sealed corner becomes blue(1) to mark \"rejected\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:31:#      maroon inside the target = packed token, gray = consumed reachable source, blue = unreachable source.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:35:#      maroon tokens, gray traces, blue rejects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:48:#    - Gray traces are only meaningful for moved sources, so generator places exactly k reachable maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:53:#      coordinate sets. Corner pockets are isolated by added wall cells before maroons are placed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:57:#      rejects, and maroon packed tokens, but the layout is still structured: blue is forced into sealed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:58:#      crop corners, gray is forced onto reachable crop cells, and maroon fill stays inside the 3x3 target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:182:    Pack reachable maroon tokens into the central 3x3 target, leave gray pickup traces, repaint blocked maroons blue, then crop to the target neighborhood.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:186:    - Magenta wall segments create corridor gaps and sealed pockets around that target, while maroon tokens sit on floor cells outside the 3x3 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:189:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the target through orange/maroon cells, then rank reachable maroons by BFS distance with row-major tie-breaks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:190:    - Move the closest reachable maroons into the 3x3 target in row-major order, turn each consumed source gray, and recolor every unreachable maroon blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:194:    - The crop hides the distant corridors, so the important evidence is local: maroon inside the 3x3 block means \"selected\", gray means \"reachable and consumed\", and blue means \"blocked out by walls\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:19:#      maroon cells, and anything beyond the 3x3 capacity simply stays outside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:24:#      If reachable maroons exceed that capacity, the spill does not stay put:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:25:#      the extra reachable maroons continue into the one-cell-thick outer ring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:29:#      If 13 reachable maroons exist, output fills the first 13 square cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:30:#      If 19 reachable maroons exist, output fills all 16 square cells and then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:33:#      extra maroons would remain at their source locations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:47:#    - \"overflow maroons are untouched\" is invalid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:56:#      never collide with walls and source/distractor maroons never start inside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:61:#    - Overflow is directly visible because the maroon fill expands from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:62:#      square into a second surrounding layer, not just \"some maroons remain\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:76:#      the square is full, the same maroon payload continues into the ring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:211:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into a variable-size square, then spill overflow into its surrounding ring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:214:    - Orange floor contains optional magenta walls and scattered maroon (9) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:218:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells touching the square, traversing only floor and maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:219:    - Sort reachable maroon pixels by BFS distance, then by row and column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:220:    - Fill the square in row-major order first; if reachable maroons still remain, continue filling the one-cell-thick outer ring around that square in row-major order. Moved maroons are erased back to floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:240:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:241:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:242:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:244:    moved = maroons[: min(len(targets), len(maroons))]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:11:#     connectivity: candidate maroons are still determined only by 4-connected flood-fill through floor/maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:14:#       old: sort reachable maroons by (bfs_distance, row, col)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:19:#       old: write the chosen maroons into the 3x3 block in row-major order\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:32:#       setup: 6 reachable maroons, all of them move\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:37:#       setup: 10 reachable maroons on the same bfs shell around the destination\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:38:#       original: 9 chosen maroons are the row-major earliest shell cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:39:#       combo: 9 chosen maroons are the clockwise-earliest shell cells from the top\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:40:#       visible_difference: the leftover outside maroon moves to a different side of the ring, even though the destination ends up full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:56:#       - walls remain hard blockers because bfs only walks on floor/maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:60:#       - generator can no longer assume \"exactly k reachable maroons\" is enough to expose every change\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:63:#       - angle-visible boards must guarantee a same-distance shell with at least 10 maroons and different row-vs-angle top-9 subsets\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:66:#     - source maroons are placed only on reachable floor cells, never inside the destination or on walls\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:67:#     - distractor maroons are placed only on unreachable floor cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:171:def _rank_reachable_maroons(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:178:    maroons = [\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:183:    maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (t[0], t[1], t[2], t[3]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:184:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:187:def _row_rank_reachable_maroons(dist: np.ndarray, maroons: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:188:    return sorted((int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in maroons)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:203:    reachable_maroons = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere((grid == 9) & (dist < 10**9))]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:204:    moved = min(len(fill_order), len(reachable_maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:205:    angle_ranked = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, dist, cr, cc)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:206:    row_ranked = _row_rank_reachable_maroons(dist, reachable_maroons)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:213:    angle_active = 1 if len(reachable_maroons) > len(fill_order) and angle_chosen != row_chosen else 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:216:        \"reachable\": len(reachable_maroons),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:224:    Move reachable maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center using clockwise tie-breaks and a spiral fill.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:227:    - Orange floor cells form the passable background, magenta walls may block parts of it, and maroon tokens sit on some floor cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:231:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination, treating floor and maroon as traversable; only reachable maroons are eligible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:232:    - Sort eligible maroons by BFS distance, then break same-distance ties by clockwise angle around the red center starting from straight up.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:233:    - Move the first nine-or-fewer maroons: erase their source cells back to floor and write them into the destination along a fixed clockwise outer-to-inner spiral.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:236:    - The same center controls both decisions: outside the block it orders tied maroons by rotation, and inside the block it lays the moved maroons down in the matching clockwise spiral.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:252:    maroons = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, dist, cr, cc)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:253:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:254:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:480:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9) if int(dist[r, c]) < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:481:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:482:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:483:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:22:#   wall opening. In a concrete example, a maroon one step outside the right\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:27:#   eight edge cells of the 3x3 block. The same right-side maroon can be ranked\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:28:#   before a farther-left maroon even if its actual corridor path is longer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:29:# - This only affects the output when there are more than 9 reachable maroons;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:30:#   otherwise every reachable maroon moves. The generator therefore guarantees\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:31:#   at least 10 reachable maroons and rejects layouts where the new top-9 set is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:42:#   maroons after the 3x3 block is filled, and those leftovers differ from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:43:#   old BFS-based choice. The user can compare \"which reachable maroons stayed\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:123:def _reachable_maroons_sorted(grid: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:126:    maroons = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:130:            maroons.append((_edge_distance(rr, cc, edge_cells), rr, cc))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:131:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:132:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:163:    Move the nine edge-nearest reachable maroon pixels into the centered 3x3 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:166:    - The board is 11x11 with orange floor, optional magenta wall barriers, scattered maroon pixels,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:173:      and maroon cells but never through magenta walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:174:    - Among the maroon pixels reached by that flood-fill, rank them by the minimum Manhattan distance\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:176:    - Move the first nine ranked maroons (or all of them if fewer exist) into the destination block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:181:    corridor length. A maroon that is geometrically close to one side of the block can outrank another\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:182:    maroon whose actual path from the center is shorter.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:194:    maroons = _reachable_maroons_sorted(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:195:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:196:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:330:    new_rank = {(r, c) for _, r, c in _reachable_maroons_sorted(probe)[:9]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:382:    reachable_maroons = _reachable_maroons_sorted(inp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:383:    if len(reachable_maroons) <= 9:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:397:    new_top9 = {(r, c) for _, r, c in reachable_maroons[:9]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/1/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形补丁+4连通邻域判定\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:14:#    - Original task ranked reachable maroons the same way as before, but then wrote them into all 9\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:20:#    - Example with k=6 reachable maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:35:#    - Generator never places walls or maroons inside the 3x3 destination block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:87:def _reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, dest_cells: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:116:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:117:    maroons = [triple for triple in maroons if triple[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:118:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:119:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:124:    Move the nearest reachable maroon pixels into the green frame around the unique red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:127:    - The board uses orange floor, optional magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and one red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:131:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the 3x3 destination block, traveling through orange or maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:132:    - Rank reachable maroon tokens by BFS distance, then by row and column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:152:    reachable = _reachable_maroons(grid, dest_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:15:      - 原题是横向条带布局: 偶数行是彩色横条, 奇数行是背景通道.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:20:      - 顶/底起点只放在真正通向边缘的竖直走廊端点; 右侧起点只放在无转弯的直通道右端, 避免逆向进入时无解.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:28:    - 仍保留 straight/L/U 三种通道类型与 fake corridor, 避免任务退化成纯直线搬运.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:54:      generator 每条路径最多一个起点, 且转弯列/通道行互异.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:3:# Name: 不可达像素向开口移动+墙壁有通道口\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:10:#       - reachable maroons are selected by BFS distance from the central 3x3 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:11:#       - maroons cut off by magenta walls are ignored and remain where they are.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:13:#       - D18/2 changes those blocked maroons into active movers that travel along the wall network.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:18:#     - Put blocked maroons in 1-cell side pockets between the two rings; each pocket touches the wall graph through two short connectors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:22:#       - a top-pocket maroon cannot be reached from the center because the top inner wall cell is closed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:25:#       - the same top-pocket maroon first attaches to adjacent magenta wall cells,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:27:#       - if that mouth is an inner opening on another side, the maroon becomes reachable and may join the central fill,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:30:#       - the new wall mouths are not cosmetic: they change both the nearest target of blocked maroons and the final ranking pool for the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:34:#     - The generator always includes both outcomes: one blocked maroon that reaches an inner opening and one that stops at an outer opening.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:37:#       - unreachable maroons can no longer be ignored before ranking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:38:#       - clearing only originally reachable sources is no longer sufficient because blocked maroons relocate first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:40:#       - blocked maroons must touch the wall graph; the generator guarantees this with side pockets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:42:#       - two blocked maroons should not compete for one target opening; the generator probes the layout and rejects collisions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:43:#       - pocket sides cannot have an inner opening on the same side, otherwise the pocket maroon would already be reachable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:46:#     - Reachable source maroons are sampled only from floor cells that are not pockets and not any potential opening cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:48:#     - The wall network is a clean square-with-frame motif, so widened mouths and moved maroons stand out immediately.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:302:def _move_blocked_maroons(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:315:    maroons = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:316:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:317:    for r, c in maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:406:    staged, moved = _move_blocked_maroons(np.asarray(grid, dtype=int), CENTER_R, CENTER_C, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:408:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(staged == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:409:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:410:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:411:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[: min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:427:    Route blocked maroon pixels to the nearest wall mouth, then fill the center block with the closest reachable maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:431:    - Magenta walls form an inner ring and an outer frame, with visible side openings of width 1 or 2 and a few maroon pixels trapped in side pockets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:434:    - First, flood-fill reachability from the destination through floor and maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:435:    - Any maroon that is still blocked travels along adjacent magenta wall cells to the nearest open wall mouth; inner mouths make it newly reachable, outer mouths only relocate it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:436:    - After those relocations, recompute reachability, rank reachable maroons by distance then row-major tie-break, and move the closest ones into the 3x3 destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:439:    - The wall openings matter twice: they are both pass-through corridors for the center flood-fill and the landing targets for previously unreachable maroons, so extra or wider mouths can change which maroons ultimately enter the block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:451:    staged, _ = _move_blocked_maroons(grid, cr, cc, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:454:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(staged == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:455:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:456:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:458:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:459:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:497:    staged_probe, moved_probe = _move_blocked_maroons(probe, CENTER_R, CENTER_C, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1ae2feb7/32/code.py:31:# - 十字形固定为半径 1 的 5 格，不引入多种模板，避免规则分叉太多。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:42:#    - Walls are written only outside dest_set. Source and distractor maroons are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:49:#      still teaches \"reachable maroons only\" before the write-path twist.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:170:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into the irregular destination shape using a spiral-with-skips fill.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:173:    - Orange floor cells may be split by magenta walls, and maroon tokens sit on some floor cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:177:    - Recover the full red+green container, then flood-fill outward through floor/maroon cells touching it to find reachable maroon candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:178:    - Rank reachable maroons by BFS distance, then by row and column, erase the closest ones from their source cells, and place them into the container.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:182:    - Two geometric inferences interact: walls still decide which maroons are eligible, but the destination is an irregular shape whose fill order is defined by a spiral on its enclosing rectangle rather than by row-major order on the shape itself.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:222:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:223:    maroons = [triple for triple in maroons if triple[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:224:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:226:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:227:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:25:#    - Example: if a blue chain goes upward from the target, a maroon sitting in a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:28:#      blue. A maroon beyond the tip of the chain is reachable, because the motion\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:57:#    - The generator always places distractor maroons inside blue-side pockets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:197:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:198:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:199:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:201:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:202:    chosen = [(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:246:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:247:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:248:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:249:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:250:    chosen = [(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:261:    Move the nearest legally reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the unique red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:264:    - Orange floor carries scattered maroon tokens, while the target is the usual 3x3 green block with one red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:269:    - Sideways turns out of a blue cell are illegal, so maroons in side pockets touching a blue ray are not reachable; reachable maroons are ranked by directed distance and then fill the target in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:23:#      Inside that square, placement is no longer row-major. The moved maroons follow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:26:#      If reachable maroons exceed the square capacity, the next maroons do not stay\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:31:#      old task with 12 reachable maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:33:#      this combo with a 4x4 square and 19 reachable maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:35:#        surrounding spill ring, and only the still-later maroons would remain outside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:36:#      this combo with a 5x5 square and 11 reachable maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:60:#    - \"overflow maroons just stay put\" is invalid. The solver must erase not only the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:61:#      maroons moved inside the square, but also the extra selected maroons moved onto\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:66:#      non-destination, non-maroon color in the whole grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:76:#    - Source maroons and distractors are sampled only from floor cells, never from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:92:#    - The generator also keeps source maroons off the spill ring in the input, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:97:#      floor, wall, green square, red anchor, maroon tokens.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:102:#    - Non-overflow samples are forced to be partial fills (at least 6 maroons and at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:105:#      extra maroons is capped to a small visible band so the spill ring activates\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:280:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into a variable-size square, and spill any excess onto the square's outer ring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:283:    - Orange floor cells may be partitioned by magenta walls, with maroon tokens scattered on reachable and unreachable floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:287:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the square, traversing only floor and maroon cells, then rank reachable maroons by BFS distance, row, and column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:288:    - Fill the square first along a clockwise inward spiral. If more ranked maroons remain after the square is full, continue by placing them on the one-cell-thick ring immediately outside the square in clockwise perimeter order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:289:    - Every moved maroon is erased from its source cell back to floor; unreachable maroons and any maroons beyond the supported spill ring remain in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:292:    - The solver must recover both the square size and the two-stage write geometry. The square size sets the internal capacity, while overflow activates a second visible path just outside the square instead of leaving extra reachable maroons on the floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:305:    reachable_maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:306:    reachable_maroons = [item for item in reachable_maroons if item[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:307:    reachable_maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:309:    inner_count = min(len(fill_path), len(reachable_maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:310:    overflow_count = min(len(spill_order), max(0, len(reachable_maroons) - inner_count))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:312:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in reachable_maroons[:moved_total]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:44:#       生成器据此避免把 BFS-only 诱饵放到开口射线的净空通道上。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:153:def _old_bfs_ranked_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, dest_set: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:298:    Move the closest maroon pixels that are directly visible through the frame openings into the central 3×3 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:302:    - The frame is mostly solid, but some non-corner side cells are single-cell openings; maroon pixels are scattered outside the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:306:    - That first blocking cell contributes only if it is maroon, so a frame opening exposes at most one candidate on that line while a wall cell blocks the ray immediately.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:310:    - The puzzle is about line of sight through explicit rectangular-frame openings, not about general corridor connectivity. A maroon pixel may still be reachable after exiting an opening, but if it requires a turn or sits behind another blocker on the same ray, it stays where it is.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:388:    ranked_old = _old_bfs_ranked_maroons(base, dest_set)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D2/1/code.py:15:   - 仍然保留原题的“偶数行是彩色条，奇数行是通道”的条纹布局，粒子仍从最左列出发。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D2/1/code.py:46:   - U 转弯仍只连接同色水平通道；目标通道入口会被破坏，避免其自身粒子也进入同一路径。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D2/1/code.py:65:   - 选择后的目标单元必须是 _has_corridor 为真的通道；builder 会显式打开该 turn cell 与延长段。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:3:# Name: 裁剪到方块区域+框架与方块有间隔通道\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:15:#    are directly adjacent to that block. Reachable maroon cells are found by BFS from the block's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:19:#      input full grid contains a 7x7 framed region plus extra outside maroons;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:22:#      after moving the closest reachable maroons into the block, the result is cropped to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:33:#    - Unreachable maroons can survive in the full grid but vanish from the final answer purely\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:44:#    hidden. Reachable maroons are visibly the ones inside the frame; outside maroons disappear\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:47:#    The three layers do not overlap: the block uses green/red, the channel uses orange/maroon, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:153:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into the central 3x3 block, then crop to the enclosing frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:156:    - The canvas contains orange floor, scattered maroon tokens, a unique red center inside a 3x3 green block,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:158:    - The frame is not adjacent to the block: a 1-2 cell orange channel separates them, and maroons may appear\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:162:    - Flood-fill from passable cells adjacent to the 3x3 block through orange/maroon cells; maroons reached by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:164:    - Sort reachable maroons by distance to the block, breaking ties by row then column, and place the closest\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:169:    Key insight: The magenta border now defines both connectivity and the crop boundary; only maroons inside the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:268:    # Independent expectation: only maroons in the inner channel are reachable because the frame is closed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/38/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形补丁+形状编码方向+冲突teal标记\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/9/code.py:25:#    - Replace the single maroon source class with multicolor single-pixel sources. This combo\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/9/code.py:39:#      dist 0-1 -> maroon(9), dist 2-3 -> gray(5), dist 4+ -> yellow(4).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/9/code.py:47:#    - The original floor-color inference relied on maroon being the only non-structural color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/39/code.py:15:  `(yellow, orange)` or `(red, maroon)`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:19:      - floor/wall/maroon color roles stay the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:21:      - reachability still uses 4-connected BFS through floor+maroon cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:22:      - each destination still fills in row-major order with its owned maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:25:      - the mapping is many:many: many maroons may feed many blocks, and a block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:26:        competes with the others for shared maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:44:      distractors: optional unreachable maroons that remain in place\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:49:      - one BFS distance map ranks all reachable maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:50:      - the first k maroons fill that single container\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:54:      - every maroon compares all reachable containers and is owned by the nearest\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:55:      - each container fills only from its owned maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:57:      - suppose a maroon lies in the central corridor and is reachable from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:81:    - original global `maroons[:k]` slice is invalid because each container has\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:88:      - merely selecting contested maroons is not enough, because the output only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:92:        input maroons than it actually owns after competition\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:94:        \"every container uses every reachable maroon independently\" reading\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:100:      - maroons are sampled only from floor cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:106:      - at least two containers receive contested maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:108:        maroons are owned by another container\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:372:    Route reachable maroon pixels into several 3x3 destination blocks around red centers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:375:    - The board is an 11x11 floor-and-wall maze with scattered maroon (9) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:379:    - For every destination block, compute BFS reachability through floor/maroon cells, stopping at walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:380:    - Each reachable maroon is owned by the nearest destination block; equal distances break by center row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:381:    - Every block sorts only its owned maroons by distance and writes them into its own 3x3 cells in row-major order, erasing the moved sources back to floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:385:    - Shared corridors create maroons that more than one block can reach, so you must compare several BFS frontiers first and only then refill each block from its assigned pool.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:408:    owned_maroons = [[] for _ in containers]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:414:        owned_maroons[owner].append((int(dists[owner][r, c]), r, c))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:417:        owned_maroons[idx].sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:418:        chosen = owned_maroons[idx][: len(dest_cells)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D8/3/code.py:3:# Change: 彩色条水平铺设在偶数行，从bar_start列延伸到网格右端；真走廊由同色条对构成，假走廊（干扰项）由异色条对构成。原版本主要靠条带/转角墙触发转向；本变体额外在走廊通道内放置孤立彩色阻挡块，粒子撞到这些单格障碍时也会转弯或停止。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D8/3/code.py:25:      - 仍然保持条纹布局: 偶数行为彩条行, 奇数行为水平通道行, 第0列全是粒子, 第1列全是背景.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D8/3/code.py:27:      - 新对象是“孤立阻挡块”: 放在通道中的单个彩色格, 不与相邻四格中的同色格连通, 视觉上明显区别于长条.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D8/3/code.py:29:        1. 水平通道内, 让粒子提前停下.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D8/3/code.py:30:        2. 水平通道拐弯口前方, 让粒子因撞块而转入竖直走廊.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D8/3/code.py:31:        3. 竖直通道内, 让粒子在竖直段中途停下.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D8/3/code.py:43:        - 旧任务里视觉上更像条带结构本身制造障碍; 新任务里单格块是独立对象, 人眼能直接看到“通道不再畅通”.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D8/3/code.py:51:    - main 的入口检测假设真实通道起点仍然由最左侧同色条对定义. 变体不能在入口左侧乱放块, 否则会把“哪几行是可追踪真实走廊”弄乱.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D8/3/code.py:56:    - 竖直停止块只放在竖直通道经过的奇数行上, 这样它是单格块, 且粒子撞到后左右都没有合法水平走廊.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D8/3/code.py:57:    - 竖直通道列仍用窗口保留法避免重叠, 各种块都不越界.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D8/3/code.py:60:    - 多个真实通道会包含这种块, 且有的导致转弯、有的导致内部停止, 规则不是偶然个例.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D8/3/code.py:62:    - 仍保持偶数行长条 + 奇数行通道的整齐结构, 只在通道内添加少量单格块.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:16:#    with a left-hand rule. Maroons on the walked route move inward; maroons in side branches stay put.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:25:# 5. Visual observability: every valid sample includes at least one maroon in a branch that BFS could reach\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:188:    Pull maroon tokens from the left-hand wall-follow route of a maze into the 3x3 block around the red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:198:    - Collect maroons encountered on that traced route, erase them from their source cells, then fill the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:202:      so branch maroons that flood-fill could reach still remain in place unless the left-hand trace actually passes through them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:216:    maroons = [(r, c) for r, c in trace_cells if int(grid[r, c]) == MAROON]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:217:    k = min(len(DEST_CELLS), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:219:    for r, c in maroons[:k]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:14:#    Example corridor: dest -> orange -> maroon A -> maroon B -> orange -> maroon C.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:15:#    Original dd6b8c4b treats maroon as passable, so A/B/C are all reachable in one BFS.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:23:#    - `passable = {floor, 9}` is no longer valid: maroon must block flood-fill.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:25:#      every collected maroon, so distances must be recomputed iteratively.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:26:#    - \"There is a passable start next to the destination\" is no longer guaranteed: a maroon can\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:27:#      sit directly at the opening, so the solver must allow direct-adjacent maroon targets even\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:34:#    marks hard obstacles, and maroon chains visibly sit inside the tunnels they block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:40:#    because some moved maroons are not initially exposed; they appear to come from behind others.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:43:#    the original \"floor+maroon are both passable\" ranking. The generator therefore measures the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:102:def _maroon_candidates(grid: np.ndarray, dest_cells: list[tuple[int, int]], dest_set: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:144:        candidates = _maroon_candidates(work, dest_cells, dest_set)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:157:    return [(r, c) for _dist, r, c in _maroon_candidates(np.asarray(grid, dtype=int), dest_cells, dest_set)[:max_take]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:161:    \"\"\"Reference helper for the original dd6b8c4b connectivity model: floor+maroon are passable.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:199:    Collect maroon tokens into the 3x3 target one at a time, recomputing reachability after each pick.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:202:    - Orange is the only traversable background; magenta walls and maroon tokens are both solid blockers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:207:    - At each step, consider maroon tokens touching that flood region (or touching the destination directly),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/3/code.py:64:#      the background away from yellow to maroon(9). This keeps all three hole bands visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/29/code.py:35:#      maroon and still mean \"go left 4\"; therefore the solver must decode motion from shape only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/21/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形补丁+边界裁剪+矩形区域\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:9:#    - solver 仍先从目标块外侧相邻的可通行单元做 flood-fill, 只把能通过 floor/maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:31:#      1. 候选排序从 `maroons.sort()` 改成按 `(-dist,row,col)`。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:45:#    - 通过限制 total maroon 数量与墙样式, 保持版面稀疏, 避免目标块附近过度拥挤。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:47:#    - 没有新增颜色语义。所有变化仍是 maroon 在 floor 与目标块之间移动。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:162:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:163:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:164:    return dest_cells, fill_order, floor, maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:170:    dest_cells, fill_order, floor, maroons = _reachable_analysis(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:173:        maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:175:        maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:178:    k = min(len(write_order), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:179:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:192:    Move the outermost reachable maroon pixels into the central 3x3 block, filling it from bottom-right backward.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:196:    - Magenta walls may carve corridors around that block, and maroon tokens are scattered on floor cells outside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:199:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination, moving only through floor or maroon cells, to find reachable maroon candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:201:    - Remove the chosen sources and place the moved maroons into the destination in reverse row-major order, starting at the lower-right corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:204:    - The same wall-gated reachability test from the original task still decides which maroons are eligible, but both downstream directions are inverted: selection prefers the farthest candidates and writing prefers the bottom-right end of the block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/800d221b/15/code.py:3:# Name: hub整体着色+十字形hub\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/4/code.py:22:#   they are enumerated in row-major scan order and colored teal, maroon, teal,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/4/code.py:23:#   maroon, ...\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/4/code.py:136:      and even-indexed centers maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/4/code.py:140:    why the center markers alternate teal-maroon-teal-maroon across the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:22:#      pixel, green around it, orange floor, optional magenta wall barriers, and maroon tokens on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:24:#    - Reachability is unchanged: only maroons connected to the destination through a 4-neighbor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:25:#      flood-fill over floor+maroon cells are eligible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:27:#      1) source ranking order = row-major scan over reachable maroons, i.e. sort by (row, col);\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:31:#      reachable maroons = {(1,8),(2,2),(8,1),(9,9),...}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:34:#      then places the moved maroons down the first column of the target before moving right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:35:#    - Because the task always moves k = min(9, reachable_count) maroons, there is an unavoidable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:37:#      * if reachable_count > 9, the source ranking is visible because some reachable maroons stay\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:39:#      * if reachable_count < 9, the column-major fill is visible, but every reachable maroon moves,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:55:#    - The original `maroons.sort()` encoded distance ranking directly. That assumption is replaced\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:56:#      with sorting reachable maroons by coordinates only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:57:#    - Floor-color inference still needs at least one visible non-maroon ring-adjacent cell. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:63:#    - Source maroons are sampled only from reachable floor cells outside the destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:70:#    - Scan-order source selection is visible through which reachable maroons remain on the floor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:74:#    - Walls still provide clear corridor structure, so reachable and unreachable maroons remain\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:78:#      among visible maroons and the fill trajectory inside the fixed 3x3 target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:89:#      and at least one visible non-maroon neighbor color around the target for floor inference.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:152:    assert cand_ring, \"ring around destination must contain at least one visible non-maroon color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:229:    Move reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 target around the unique red center, ranking by scan position and filling by columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:236:    - Flood-fill from passable cells adjacent to the destination through floor and maroon cells to determine which maroon pixels are reachable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:237:    - Ignore path distance when ordering those reachable maroons: sort them only by row first, then column, erase the first up to nine source cells, and place those maroons into the destination in column-major order from the top-left.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:238:    - Destination cells beyond the moved count keep their original green/red colors, and unreachable maroons remain unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:241:    - The problem separates eligibility from placement: walls still decide which maroons can move, but once reachability is known the source order is a global scan order while the destination uses a different, column-first traversal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/8/code.py:26:#    - D3/1 breaks the old color-shape binding: a plus may be orange, teal, maroon, etc.,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/8/code.py:31:#        glyphs in reading order = cross(teal), plus(maroon), diamond(teal), plus(orange)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:8:# - Baseline dd6b8c4b: the magenta barrier hugs the 3x3 green/red destination. Reachable maroons are found by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:9:#   floor BFS from cells immediately outside the block; maroons trapped behind the wall are ignored and stay put.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:14:# - D18/2 change: blocked maroons are not static distractors. Each trapped maroon sits in a sealed 1-cell pocket\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:17:#   recompute which maroons are reachable from the center block and fill the block by distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:18:# - Example trace: a maroon in the left-upper pocket at (3,1) is surrounded by wall on all four sides, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:20:#   is open, the maroon follows the frame around the top-left corner to the top opening at (0,5). From that new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:27:# - Pockets are single-cell chambers, so each moved maroon has a unique origin. Openings are one cell wide and are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:29:# - The generator enforces 2-3 moving maroons, at least one moved maroon that later fills the center block, at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:30:#   least one moved maroon that remains visible at an opening, and a wall-path length threshold. This prevents the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:36:# - Original assumption: unreachable maroons can be ignored forever. Broken by D18/2. Now they may become reachable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:38:# - Original assumption: clearing only the chosen reachable source cells is sufficient. Broken because moved maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:41:#   1. Every trapped maroon is adjacent to at least one wall cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:43:#   3. Different trapped maroons are assigned distinct nearest openings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:51:# - Reachable source maroons are sampled only from orange floor cells that are not pockets and not opening slots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:55:#   is the D14 part. They can also see maroons disappear from sealed side pockets and reappear on border openings,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:62:#   a handful of isolated pocket/source maroons. No region carries multiple kinds of markup on top of each other.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:63:# - Because pockets are tiny and sparse, the output does not become cluttered even when one moved maroon remains on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:64:#   the frame while other maroons fill the center block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:68:#   behavior, if at least two blocked maroons actually move along the frame, and if the moved maroons exhibit both\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:187:def _move_blocked_maroons(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:198:    maroons = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:199:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:200:    for r, c in maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:240:def _select_reachable_maroons(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:245:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:246:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:247:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:248:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:249:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:250:    return maroons, chosen\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:254:    maroons, chosen = _select_reachable_maroons(grid, dest_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:255:    _ = maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:266:    Route trapped maroons along a detached border frame, then use the closest reachable maroons to fill the center block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:271:    - Some maroons are ordinary reachable floor tokens, while others sit inside tiny sealed pockets attached to the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:274:    - First, detect maroons that are unreachable from the center through orange/maroon floor travel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:275:    - Each such blocked maroon moves along the connected magenta frame to the nearest valid side-center opening.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:276:    - After all blocked maroons relocate, recompute reachability and move the closest reachable maroons into the 3x3 block in row-major order, erasing the selected source positions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:291:    staged, _ = _move_blocked_maroons(grid, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:292:    _maroons, chosen = _select_reachable_maroons(staged, dest_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:339:    staged, moved = _move_blocked_maroons(np.asarray(grid, dtype=int), dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:340:    _maroons, chosen = _select_reachable_maroons(staged, dest_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:398:    staged_probe, moved_probe = _move_blocked_maroons(probe, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:3:# Name: 8连通可达+墙壁通道口+规则框架\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:16:#      green 3x3 target block and moves through floor/maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:48:#    - At least one blocked mouth exists, and at least four maroons lie in the 8-only reachable set.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:162:    maroons = [\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:167:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:169:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:170:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:181:    Move the nearest 8-reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:192:      maroon pixels as passable and magenta as blocking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:193:    - Collect only maroon pixels reached by that 8-connected search.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:194:    - Sort reachable maroons by distance, then row, then column, and copy the closest ones into\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:250:    maroon_cells = {(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:251:    only8_maroons = maroon_cells & (reach8 - reach4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:258:        \"only8_maroons\": len(only8_maroons),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:260:        \"nearest_only8_dist\": min((int(dist8[r, c]) for r, c in only8_maroons), default=-1),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:292:    if metrics[\"only8_maroons\"] < FILL_RANGE[0] or metrics[\"output_diff\"] <= 0:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/36/code.py:28:#     a 5x5 or 7x7 opposite-color patch and its center becomes maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/36/code.py:33:#     combo emits 7x7 in color B with a maroon center. Size and center color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/36/code.py:41:#     d==1, otherwise maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/36/code.py:76:#   - Foreground colors never use teal or maroon, so the center markers remain\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/36/code.py:221:      larger radius, recolor its center maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/36/code.py:225:    make larger patches with maroon centers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/36/code.py:452:    has_maroon = any(int(radius) >= 2 for _r, _c, _host, radius in selected)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/36/code.py:453:    if not (has_teal and has_maroon):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/29/code.py:27:#     to one shared color (maroon 9). The output no longer preserves the input frame colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/29/code.py:41:#     generator excludes black(0) and maroon(9) from interiors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/29/code.py:214:    - After moving, every square border is recolored to the same maroon value, so output borders\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:36:#   reachable maroons, so the destination can only accept a subset.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:39:#   maroon back to inferred floor\". All three are unsafe now. This solver uses a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:41:#   generator guarantees every maroon sits on an orange endpoint so erasing a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:64:    MAROON: 1,  # generator places maroons on orange corridor endpoints\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:166:def _rank_reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, *, weighted: bool) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:186:    ranked = _rank_reachable_maroons(g, weighted=True)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:199:    Move the lowest-cost reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the unique red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:204:    - Orange and grey corridor cells are both traversable; scattered maroon pixels sit on corridor endpoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:207:    - Start from corridor cells adjacent to the destination block and search through orange, grey, and maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:208:    - Entering orange or maroon costs 1, while entering grey costs 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:209:    - Rank reachable maroons by total path cost, breaking ties by row then column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:210:    - Move the best-ranked maroons into the destination in row-major order and erase their source cells back to orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:241:    weighted = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, weighted=True)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:242:    plain = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, weighted=False)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D13/0/code.py:24:#     - 设源通道 A 在更上方，源通道 B 在其下方，二者都通过各自的 U-turn 进入同一目标通道 T。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D13/0/code.py:46:#   - 特制级联结构使用两个上方源通道 + 一个下方目标通道，中间插入一个 fake spacer channel，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D13/0/code.py:47:#     防止 target 入口被打断后反过来破坏紧邻上方源通道的入口合法性。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D13/0/code.py:48:#   - 两个源通道使用不同的垂直列进入同一目标通道，肉眼能直接看到“共享尾段”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/16/code.py:20:#      red (2) => original-looking palette, maroon (9) => alternate palette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/16/code.py:23:#      background and receives an inner outline; if its outer marker is maroon that outline turns\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/16/code.py:24:#      maroon instead of red and the kept/recolored body uses the alternate palette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/16/code.py:175:      away is red (2) or maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:23:#    - D13/2 then changes what happens when too few reachable maroons exist:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:24:#      the solver still ranks reachable maroons by BFS distance, but if fewer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:28:#      input square = 5x5, reachable maroons = 6.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:29:#      Old D6-only logic: place 6 maroons into the first 6 cells of the full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:31:#      Fused logic: 6 maroons need only a 3x3 square, so the output keeps only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:33:#      with maroon, leaves the remaining 3 cells green, and turns the removed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:47:#    - \"moved maroons fill exactly the visible input container\" is invalid;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:70:#    - Walls remain external; maroons remain on floor in the input, so objects\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:75:#    - The only count-based step is human-visible: count the reachable maroons,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:92:#    - Assumption: there is at least one reachable maroon in accepted samples,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:94:#      Generator: chooses at least 5 reachable source maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:221:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into a variable square container, then shrink that container when the moved count is too small.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:224:    - Orange floor contains optional magenta walls and scattered maroon (9) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:228:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the square, traversing only floor and maroon cells, then rank reachable maroons by BFS distance with row-major tie-breaking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:229:    - Move as many ranked maroons as possible, capped by the input square area. If that moved count is smaller than the input capacity, rebuild the destination as the smallest anchored square that can hold those moved maroons; otherwise keep the original square size.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:230:    - Clear the moved source maroons back to floor, fill the final square in row-major order with the moved maroons, and leave any unused cells inside that final square as green/red container cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:233:    - The visible input square is only an upper bound on capacity. The solver must first detect the whole anchored square, then count how many maroons are actually reachable, because that count determines whether the output stays full-size or collapses to a smaller square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:244:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:245:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:246:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:249:    moved_count = min(capacity, len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:250:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:moved_count]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/25/code.py:53:#     - a hidden object with outer border 4 and inner 3x3 maroon 9 at row 14 / col 15 looks like a plain 3x3 maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:16:#    floor, magenta walls, and maroon tokens outside the block. The original task only erased chosen\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:17:#    reachable maroons and refilled the destination block. Here the same BFS ranking still chooses the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:19:#    the farthest reachable maroon distance. A shortest path from each collected source to the block is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:41:#    The generator never places maroons inside the destination block or on walls. Corridor branches stay\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:57:#    reachable maroons still fill the destination in distance order, the farthest reachable maroon sets\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:240:    Pull reachable maroon pixels into the central 3×3 block, stretch space around that block, and show teal transport routes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:243:    - The input still uses the original 11×11 vocabulary: orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and a fixed green 3×3 destination with one red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:244:    - Openings beside the destination lead into floor corridors; only maroons connected through those corridors are reachable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:247:    - Flood-fill from passable cells adjacent to the destination, treating floor and maroon as passable, then sort reachable maroons by BFS distance and by row/column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:248:    - Let the farthest reachable maroon distance be the expansion width; output a larger canvas formed by inserting that many floor rows and columns around the destination block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:249:    - Move the closest reachable maroons into the destination in row-major order, erase their source cells, and paint every floor cell on each chosen BFS route teal, including the stretched bridge through the inserted bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:252:    - The same connectivity-and-distance rule decides which maroons are collected, but solving the combo now requires two extra inferences: reconstructing predecessor paths for the trail, and remapping the whole scene into a larger coordinate system whose added width depends on the farthest reachable maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:267:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:268:    reachable = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:270:    assert reachable, \"there must be at least one reachable maroon token\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D18/0/code.py:3:# Change: 装饰条是放在假走廊通道中的单个彩色像素，作为纯视觉干扰项，不影响粒子移动。... → 装饰条作为方向提示\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:21:#    everything. So the reachable maroon set depends on both where the search is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:29:#    - There is no single floor color anymore, so erased maroons cannot be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:178:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:179:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:180:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:181:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:182:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:193:    Pull the nearest direction-reachable maroon tokens into the 3x3 target around the red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:206:    - Reachable maroon cells are ranked by directed distance, then by row and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:208:    - Each moved maroon is erased back to the stripe background color of its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:216:    maroons can actually reach the target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/27/code.py:45:#     The generator therefore reserves maroon(9) for the output border and black(0) for bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:40:#    Original output only moved reachable maroon tokens into the 3x3 target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:42:#    maroons, but its hidden BFS footprint becomes visible: every reachable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:44:#    unreachable maroon distractor turns blue(1). Example: if a maroon sits\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:45:#    behind a wall arm, original output left it maroon; new output recolors it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:47:#    maroons are still removed, but their cells now become trail color rather\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:51:#    reachable path/background, 1 means rejected maroon. This is enough to make\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:60:#    It also cannot assume all non-moved maroons stay maroon: unreachable ones\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:69:#    connected region from the target openings, while rejected blue maroons sit\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:71:#    visible because only the closest reachable maroons are transferred into the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:82:#    non-empty unreachable floor, and at least one unreachable maroon so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:240:    Move the nearest reachable maroon pixels into the center block, while exposing the reachability map.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:243:    - The board uses orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and a unique red center inside a 3x3 green destination block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:247:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells adjacent to the destination, using orange and maroon cells as the traversable medium.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:248:    - Sort reachable maroon tokens by BFS distance, then by row and column; move the closest ones into the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:249:    - In the output, every reachable floor location is recolored to the trail color, chosen source tokens disappear into that trail, and unreachable maroon tokens are recolored blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:252:    - The destination fill still depends on the same reachability-and-distance logic as the original task, but this variant also paints the whole reachable component and explicitly marks rejected maroons, turning the hidden flood-fill partition into visible evidence.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:266:    reachable_maroons = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:267:    unreachable_maroons = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:272:            reachable_maroons.append(item)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:274:            unreachable_maroons.append((int(r), int(c)))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:275:    reachable_maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:277:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(reachable_maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:278:    chosen_sources = {(r, c) for _, r, c in reachable_maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:284:    for r, c in unreachable_maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/1/code.py:3:# Name: 连接器配对十字形标记+方向标记\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:28:#    - 原题的 `maroons.sort()` 默认是最近优先；这里必须改成距离降序，否则 D3/0 不生效。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:35:#    - 生成器先在仅 floor 的距离图上选近层/远层候选，再把这些 floor 位置改成 maroon，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:47:#    - 新规则不引入新的颜色种类，只重排已有 maroon / green / red 的出现位置。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:169:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:170:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:171:    return dest_cells, fill_slots, floor, maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:177:    dest_cells, fill_slots, floor, maroons = _analyze_grid(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:180:        maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:182:        maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:185:    k = min(len(target_slots), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:186:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:199:    Move the farthest reachable maroon pixels into a checkerboard subset of the 3x3 block around the lone red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:202:    - The board is an orange floor with optional magenta walls and scattered maroon source pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:206:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination, walking only through floor or maroon cells, and keep only reachable maroon pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:208:    - Move the selected maroons into the destination's row-major odd positions only, which forms a checkerboard pattern; the even positions keep their original green/red contents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:211:    - The walls still determine reachability, but the visible output now combines two independent cues: source removal prefers the outermost reachable maroons, and the target block only accepts them on alternating checkerboard cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/1/code.py:14:#     reason_for_sidebar: 原题 col0 是粒子列、col1 是通道前的缓冲列，不能拿来编码；把编码挪到最右侧最稳妥，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/1/code.py:33:#     - 每张图仍保留 3-6 条真实通道，且至少 2 条路径被步数上限截断，至少 1 条在拐弯后才被截断，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/1/code.py:48:#     - 侧栏墙色不参与任何走廊颜色集合，solver 也把入口搜索限制在走廊区，因此不会把侧栏误判为通道。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/19/code.py:42:#    cyan/maroon pixels. Across examples, that local divider cue flips whether the first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:14:#    The original task used a centered 3x3 destination and maroon tokens scattered anywhere on floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:16:#    Maroon sources are no longer interior speckles: every movable or distracting maroon lies on the outer border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:19:#    which maroons qualify, but now the candidate pool itself is visibly \"edge only\" and strongly asymmetric.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:22:#    positional change from a few examples. Border-only maroons are a strong visual cue, and the wall layout uses\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:26:#    - Collectible maroons are filtered to border cells only; interior maroons, if present, are ignored as sources.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:30:#    The chosen centers keep the full 5x5 wall frame in-bounds. Walls, destination cells, and border maroons occupy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:31:#    disjoint cell sets, and all source/distractor maroons are sampled only from floor border cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:33:#    In 2-4 examples, a solver can see that maroons only appear on the boundary and that the block sits off-center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:34:#    Which border maroons move is explained by visible corridors/openings rather than invisible bookkeeping.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:36:#    Each role has its own region: the 3x3 target, a magenta wall frame, and edge-only maroons. This avoids the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:39:#    No new color remapping is introduced. The only semantic change is positional: \"border maroons reachable through\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:184:    Move the nearest reachable border maroons into the off-center 3x3 block around the red pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:188:    - Maroon source pixels appear only on the outer border of the grid; some border maroons may be cut off by walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:191:    - Find the unique red cell, take its surrounding 3x3 as the destination, then flood-fill outward through floor and maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:192:    - Only border maroons reached by that flood-fill are candidates; sort them by BFS distance, then row, then column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:196:    - The asymmetry comes from two places at once: candidate maroons live only on the border, and the target block sits closer to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:197:      some borders than others. Visible wall barriers decide which border sides can actually contribute maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:238:    maroons = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:243:            maroons.append((int(dist[r, c]), r, c))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:244:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:246:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:247:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/3/code.py:33:#    输入输出会退化成原题。因此 generator 强制至少 2 条真实入口通道在中途变成短假走廊补丁，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/3/code.py:34:#    让新终点在 2-4 个样例里肉眼可见。其余通道仍保留直行 / L / U 的原始风格，避免任务过度简化。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/3/code.py:36:#    - 入口筛选依赖“最左侧真正可进入的通道在起始列附近必须是同色条对”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/3/code.py:43:#    真实入口通道选择为“尽量互不相邻”的奇数行通道，原因是相邻通道共享一条横条。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/3/code.py:44:#    假终点补丁要改写某一侧横条的颜色；若两个活动真通道相邻，会互相破坏对方的结构。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/3/code.py:50:#    假终点补丁只在单条活动水平通道上做 2-4 列短色块，不叠加额外标记，不改变粒子颜色，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/3/code.py:51:#    仍保留清晰的条带结构。活动通道彼此隔开，减少共享边界导致的视觉噪声。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/3/code.py:60:#    - trace 假设入口通道起步是真走廊；generator 保证 bar_start 到补丁前保持同色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/3/code.py:61:#    - main 仍可能在多粒子场景下并行写输出；generator 通过分离通道与唯一终点设计，避免两个粒子争同一终点。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:23:#    - Reachability still uses 4-neighbor BFS through floor/maroon cells, but a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:24:#      maroon is moved only if it lies within the number of BFS layers unlocked\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:27:#      old: fixed 3x3, all reachable maroons compete for 9 cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:28:#      new 4x4: only distance<=1 maroons are moved, and output becomes 6x6.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:29:#      new 5x5: distance<=2 maroons are moved, and output becomes 9x9.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:34:#    - Generators force at least one moved maroon on the outermost unlocked BFS\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:35:#      layer and at least one farther reachable maroon that remains, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:50:#    - Distractor maroons are sampled outside the final expanded square so they\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:55:#    - The output visibly shows a larger green/maroon square, revealing that the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:57:#    - Farther reachable maroons remain on the floor, so the growth cutoff is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:62:#    - Walls and leftover maroons remain outside the final container, avoiding\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:72:#    - Each accepted grid must have at least one moved maroon on the last growth\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:73:#      layer and at least one still-reachable maroon beyond that layer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:82:#    - Assumption: leftover maroons outside the moved set are outside the final\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:199:    Grow a variable-size square container outward and move only the maroons reached within its growth depth.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:202:    - Orange floor contains optional magenta walls and scattered maroon (9) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:206:    - Flood-fill through floor and maroon cells from the square's outside edge, measuring 4-neighbor BFS distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:207:    - The square expands by a size-dependent number of rings: 4x4 grows by 1 ring, 5x5 grows by 2 rings. Move only the maroons within those unlocked BFS layers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:208:    - Erase moved maroons to floor, replace the expanded square by green, then write the collected maroons into that expanded square in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:225:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:226:    chosen = [(d, r, c) for d, r, c in maroons if d <= rounds]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/3/code.py:23:#   * decorations use one separate input color: maroon `9`;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/3/code.py:31:#     front, so blue/red are blocking and maroon is passable immediately. A maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/3/code.py:50:#   red, and maroon coexist.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/3/code.py:51:# - \"All non-bg wall pixels should block the first flood\" is invalid because maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/3/code.py:73:# - The same maroon decoration color is shown on both sides of the barrier: reachable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/3/code.py:74:#   maroon stays maroon, hidden maroon turns gray. That makes the D6 recolor rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/3/code.py:89:#   * hidden maroon decor -> gray\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/2/code.py:10:#     - 起始时粒子位于最左列，但一旦进入横向通道，计作第 1 段走廊。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/2/code.py:17:#     - 输入布局仍是偶数行条带 / 奇数行水平通道，垂直通道仍由 bar-row 上打洞形成。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/2/code.py:27:#     - U/S 型路径（至少 3 段）会比原题少走最后一段，因此终点常落在网格内部的竖直通道末端。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/2/code.py:38:#   - main() 的入口检测假设真实通道从列 2/3 附近开始，且上下条带同色；变体不改入口定义，仍成立。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/2/code.py:42:#   - generator 仍使用不重叠的竖直通道列窗口分配，避免两个转弯结构共享同一竖井。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:19:#   with a red center and green ring, orange floor, magenta walls, and many maroon tokens outside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:22:#   2. Among reachable maroons, the chosen movers are ordered by Euclidean distance to the block center,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:31:# - Important difference from the original generator: if there are <= 9 reachable maroons, every reachable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:33:#   reachable maroons so the 9-cell capacity forces a visible keep-vs-move selection.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:37:# - Use 10-14 reachable maroons and at most 0-3 unreachable distractors. This is enough to expose the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:48:#   Broken by D3/2. The new solver must compute reachability by flood-fill but rank selected maroons by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:50:# - Original assumption hidden in the old generator: reachable maroon count can be 2-9.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:52:#   The new generator guarantees more reachable maroons than capacity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:57:# - The destination block is fixed at rows 4-6 and cols 4-6; source maroons are placed only on floor cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:64:# - Because only 9 of 10-14 reachable maroons move, some reachable maroons remain outside in the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:73:# - Distractors are limited and optional. Most of the visual signal comes from the reachable maroons around\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:78:# - The green ring must stay passable; generator never replaces it with walls or maroons in the input.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:169:def _reachable_maroons_from_center(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], np.ndarray, list[tuple[int, int]]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:172:    maroons = [\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:177:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:178:    return center, dist, maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:182:    center, _dist, maroons = _reachable_maroons_from_center(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:183:    ranked = sorted(maroons, key=lambda rc: (_euclid2(center, rc), rc[0], rc[1]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:188:    _center, dist, maroons = _reachable_maroons_from_center(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:189:    ranked = sorted(maroons, key=lambda rc: (int(dist[rc[0], rc[1]]), rc[0], rc[1]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:197:    maroons = [\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:202:    ranked = sorted(maroons, key=lambda rc: (int(dist[rc[0], rc[1]]), rc[0], rc[1]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:222:    center, dist_center, reachable = _reachable_maroons_from_center(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:247:    Move the selected reachable maroons into the centered 3x3 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:255:      and maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:256:    - Keep only the reachable maroons, then rank them by Euclidean distance to the block center, breaking ties\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:258:    - Move up to nine ranked maroons into the destination block in row-major order and erase only those sources.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/23/code.py:41:#       - an orange hollow object becomes maroon with a green outline\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/23/code.py:96:    7: 9,  # orange -> maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/0/code.py:10:#    - 主体迷宫仍是原题的横条纹走廊：偶数行是彩条，奇数行是粒子通道；粒子从最左列向右进入。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/0/code.py:16:#    - 原题在一个水平通道里遇到阻挡色块时，只会存在一个可转的垂直口；本变体则把上/下两个口都打开，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/0/code.py:37:#    - 竖向通道仍使用原生成器的 vcol 预留窗口，避免不同转弯共用同一列导致串线。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/0/code.py:39:#      不会跨区域干扰别的通道。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:18:#    - Replace the single maroon source class with 2-3 token colors drawn from a small fixed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:25:#        distance order      = [(d0,blue), (d1,maroon), (d2,blue), (d3,yellow)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:26:#        grouped order       = [(blue,d0), (blue,d2), (yellow,d3), (maroon,d1)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:28:#      Original task would have written a uniform maroon row-major prefix; this combo instead\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:39:#    - `passable = {floor, 9}` breaks because movable tokens are no longer all maroon; now every\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:46:#    - Original floor inference from \"the only other color is maroon\" is unsafe with multi-color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/6/code.py:57:#      borders, and hollow shells chosen from teal/gray/maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/6/code.py:69:    7: 9,  # orange -> maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:18:#   - Replace the old \"all reachable maroons are already passable, then sort once by distance\" rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:21:#       2. A maroon cell is collected when it sits on the current BFS frontier, i.e. it is 4-neighbor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:23:#       3. Collected maroons turn into floor, so the reachable floor region expands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:24:#       4. Repeat layer by layer until the 3x3 destination is full or no frontier maroons remain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:25:#   - This makes maroon cells behave like removable gate tokens instead of already-open corridor cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:29:#       * Treat floor and maroon as passable from the start.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:31:#       * Sort every reachable maroon by raw BFS distance and move the closest ones.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:34:#       * Just beyond that opening, one maroon gate blocks access to the first annulus.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:35:#       * After removing that gate, the first annulus becomes reachable; maroons sitting in that annulus\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:39:#       * Reachability is no longer static. A farther maroon that is \"close\" under the original solver\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:42:#         gate maroon that must be peeled away before the next depth becomes reachable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:48:#     maroons, so the solver must reason about both partial final-layer filling and nested unlocking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:49:#   - The generator prefers far-from-entry maroons in inner annuli and near-entry maroons in outer annuli,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:57:#   - The original assumption \"maroon is globally passable\" is no longer valid. The combo solver must BFS\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:68:#   - Gate maroons are reserved on floor cells known to be inside bounds and not in the destination block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:69:#   - Source maroons are sampled from disjoint floor-cell candidate sets; distractors, when used, are sampled\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:73:#   - A human sees nested magenta frames with different opening sides, plus maroons clustered by depth.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:74:#   - The output effect is not just \"take the closest maroons\": inner gate tokens disappear first, then the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:346:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:347:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:348:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:349:    chosen = [(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[: len(dest_cells)]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:375:    Pull maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the red center by unlocking the nested frames layer by layer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:384:    - At each step, collect every maroon that lies on the current BFS frontier, in row-major order; the collected maroons become floor, which may open the next annulus.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:385:    - Continue outward layer by layer until the destination block is full or no frontier maroons remain, then place the collected maroons into the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:387:    Key insight: The nested magenta frames do not just filter static reachability. Their openings create a sequence of locked annuli, and maroon gates must be removed in BFS layers before farther maroons can even become candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/2/code.py:14:#   对 U 转弯的第二次拐弯，红点在目标横向走廊与竖直通道的交点 `(target_row, vcol)`。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/2/code.py:49:# - 控制点只出现在走廊中心线，不放在彩条上，也不做多色图例；视觉层次仍是“彩条/橙色通道/红点/品红粒子”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/30/code.py:32:#      这样同一个 glyph 同时暴露“方向通道”和“长度/输出色通道”，但真正的长度仍由面积给出。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:3:# Name: 通道宽度约束洪填+迷宫墙壁\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:17:#    The original task only moved reachable maroon tokens into the fixed 3x3 destination and erased\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:22:#    - within that region, the actual predecessor chains that carry chosen maroons back to the target\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:35:#      chosen maroons back into floor. That no longer holds; reachable background must also change.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:40:#      reachable branch with no maroon source, so some explored cells remain yellow-only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:45:#    maroons are placed on isolated floor pockets outside the corridor network.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:48:#    untouched walls stay magenta, unreachable pockets stay orange/maroon, all reachable background\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:57:#    carries collected maroons\". The generator enforces both roles in every accepted sample.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:180:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:181:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:182:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:184:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:185:    chosen = [(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:206:    Gather reachable maroon pixels into the central 3x3 block and visualize both the explored region and the transport routes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:209:    - The board contains orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and a fixed green 3x3 destination with one red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:210:    - Passable openings beside the destination lead into corridor-like floor regions; isolated floor pockets may hold unreachable distractor maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:213:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination, treating orange floor and maroon tokens as passable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:214:    - Rank reachable maroons by flood-fill distance, then by row and column; the closest ones fill the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:215:    - In the output, every reachable floor cell becomes yellow to show the explored background, while the actual floor cells on each chosen source-to-destination parent chain are recolored teal; chosen source maroons themselves disappear back to orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:218:    - The fill order is still controlled by reachability and distance, but the fused variant exposes two nested BFS products: the full reachable background region and the narrower subset of floor cells that lie on the transport routes of the collected maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/2/code.py:44:# - 假走廊通过“更宽的缺口/更高的通道”制造干扰，但不会和真走廊重叠到难以辨认。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:19:#      keep only reachable maroons, sort them by BFS step distance, then place\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:20:#      the chosen maroons into the 3x3 block in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:23:#      1. Mark every reachable maroon with its BFS reachability information.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:24:#      2. Re-sort those marked maroons by Euclidean distance to the red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:34:#      only when there are more than 9 reachable maroons.  Then the top-9 set\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:35:#      itself can differ, changing which scattered maroons disappear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:38:#    - The generator forces >9 reachable maroons and requires the Euclidean\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:48:#    - \"only orange floor and maroon are passable\": unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:56:#    - Generator places maroons only on floor cells, never inside the 3x3 block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:59:#      sources, leftover reachable maroons, and distractors never overlap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:62:#    - A human can see the distinction because some maroons that are geometrically\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:64:#      farther maroon that stays behind.  The walls provide the visible reason\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:71:#      red center, maroon tokens.  No extra marks are added.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:73:#      barrier network, scattered maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:138:def _mark_reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, dest_cells: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:147:def _sort_marked_maroons(marked: list[tuple[int, int, int]], center_r: int, center_c: int) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:165:    Pull reachable maroons into the central 3x3 block, but separate marking,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:175:    - Phase 1 marks every maroon that is reachable through 4-connected floor or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:176:      maroon cells starting from passable cells adjacent to the target block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:177:    - Phase 2 reorders only those marked maroons by Euclidean distance to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:179:    - Phase 3 moves the first nine (or fewer) maroons from that Euclidean list:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:185:      longer depends on corridor length.  A maroon that is geometrically close\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:186:      to the center can outrank a path-shorter maroon if walls force a detour.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:195:    marked = _mark_reachable_maroons(grid, dest_cells)   # phase 1: mark\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:196:    ordered = _sort_marked_maroons(marked, cr, cc)       # phase 2: sort\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/21/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形标记+多尺寸变体+方向标记像素\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D20/1/code.py:3:# Change: 走廊支持0-3次转弯：直通（0转）、L形（1转）、U形（2转，同色通道由垂直条连接）。... → Z形走廊（连续两次同向转弯）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/15/code.py:41:#       Suppose TL input uses {orange anchor, teal, pink, maroon}; TR anchor is green,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D20/2/code.py:3:# Change: 走廊支持0-3次转弯：直通（0转）、L形（1转）、U形（2转，同色通道由垂直条连接）。... → 螺旋走廊（3次以上转弯）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D5/1/code.py:3:# Change: 源为8像素的空心菱形轮廓（5x5外接矩形中的对角线位置像素）... → 十字形（加号形状）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D11/1/code.py:3:# Change: 严格条纹布局——偶数行为条行，奇数行为通道行/背景行；输出与输入同尺寸。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/36a08778/33/code.py:3:# Name: 缺口穿透+通道宽度约束\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/32/code.py:61:#    - 1 像素框 + 1 像素黑间隔使不同圈层不会糊在一起；十字只占中心十字形通道，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D13/0/code.py:62:  - 交互集中在一对菱形的一条对角通道上，不把全图做成大面积交叉网\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/23/code.py:40:#   combo target input: a 3x3 red anchor plus a few stray teal/maroon pixels nearby.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/4/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形精灵+旋转放入\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/12/code.py:29:#    Example: with slot colors [blue, red, yellow, maroon] and input heights\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/4/code.py:14:#      之后直行步长推广为 3/2（即 spacing+1 / spacing），于是同心矩形通道之间始终隔 2 格；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/4/code.py:24:#      第一条侧向通道会离十字主横/主竖条过近，无法满足“留白=L”的新规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/4/code.py:29:#    - 人类可以直接从样例里同时读出两件事：靠近中心的首条横/竖通道与十字之间的空隙就是 L；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/23/code.py:38:#         marker_color, grey(5), maroon(9) repeated radius times, then bg padding\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/23/code.py:43:#         pink + 1 个 maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/23/code.py:44:#         yellow + 2 个 maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/23/code.py:45:#         blue + 3 个 maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/23/code.py:46:#         orange + 4 个 maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/23/code.py:79:#   - legend 使用 grey 分隔和 maroon tally，和 red bar / green path / azure bg 层次分明。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/23/code.py:180:    - One corner contains a 4-row legend: each row shows a marker color, a grey separator, and 1-4 maroon tally cells that explicitly define that color's distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/18/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形锚点 + 空心框锚点\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/43/code.py:13:#      bar above, a yellow bar below, a teal bar left, and a maroon bar right. The old rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/25/code.py:36:#        red > teal > yellow > blue > maroon > grey\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/25/code.py:37:#      那么 9->red, 1->teal, 6->yellow, 2->blue, 8->maroon, 4->grey,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/25/code.py:39:#        (red, blue), (teal, maroon), (yellow, grey)。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/11/code.py:19:#    maroon -> pink -> gray -> blue -> teal -> green. Example with three pieces:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/11/code.py:21:#    [maroon, pink, gray] confirm that same order after translation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/97d7923e/16/code.py:236:CAP_POOL = (1, 3, 5, 9)  # blue, green, grey, maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形锚点 + 连接方向由锚点决定\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/25/code.py:3:# Name: 连通分量计数+行列互换+多色控制通道\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/25/code.py:23:#          另一个颜色只在本象限出现，充当干扰通道。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/25/code.py:24:#       2) D1/2: 真正控制尺寸的不是像素数，而是这条共享颜色通道在该象限里的 4 邻接连通分量数。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/25/code.py:34:#     - 若左右控制区都有许多共同颜色，人类难以判断目标通道；因此限制为“恰有一个共享颜色 +\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/25/code.py:50:#       “先分离颜色通道”的结构线索。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/25/code.py:56:#     - 每个控制象限只用两种非黑色，避免上方通道过多导致画面嘈杂。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/32/code.py:35:#        to its right at clearly different distances. The farthest bar is maroon, then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/32/code.py:38:#        from the teal seed, in the order maroon -> orange -> blue -> green.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/2/code.py:48:#   {grey=5, pink=6, orange=7, teal=8, maroon=9}. This keeps connectors easy to isolate by eye.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/17/code.py:17:      legend display colors are {yellow, teal, maroon}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/17/code.py:19:      source task output would be [yellow, maroon, background]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:24:#   original: 5-pixel plus -> phase tile -> always 16x16 lattice -> centered 6x6 maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:25:#   variant:  5-pixel plus -> phase tile -> 15x15 lattice -> centered 6x6 maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:62:# - The output still has only two layers: a repeated orange/black lattice and a centered maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:69:#   color; output uses only black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:121:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a variable-size periodic lattice whose side length is set by the glyph's pixel count, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:131:    - Fill that canvas by tiling the phase tile, then place a centered 6x6 maroon stamp made from a 2x2 tiling of the original glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:20:      - Keep the original 2x2 maroon stamp of the 3x3 glyph, so the stamp is still 6x6.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:36:    - Overwriting lattice cells with maroon is still safe because the original task already allowed the stamp to cover the lattice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:43:    - A left/right or top/bottom shift is immediately visible because the maroon stamp is large and contrasts with the orange/black lattice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:94:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice and place the maroon 2x2 stamp at a location derived from the glyph's input position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:104:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2, recolor its True cells to maroon, and treat that as a 6x6 stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:108:    - The glyph's shape still chooses the lattice phase, but the glyph's position in the 6x6 input now also encodes where the maroon stamp belongs on the 16x16 output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/40/code.py:3:# Name: 模板色由控制位置决定+多色控制通道\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:16:#   structure is the 6x6 maroon stamp made by tiling the glyph 2x2: instead of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:21:#   In the source task, a plus glyph always produced the same centered maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:23:#   but its 6x6 maroon overlay starts at (0,0). Likewise an H still decodes to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:40:#   Overlap with the orange/black lattice is intentional and safe because maroon is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:43:#   The maroon overlay is large and isolated, so moving it from center to a corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:118:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour motif into a 16x16 periodic lattice with the motif stamped in maroon at a glyph-specific corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:128:    - Tile the input glyph 2x2 into a 6x6 maroon stamp, then place that stamp in a corner chosen by glyph type rather than at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:131:    - The input object still serves as a code for two output attributes: its contour determines the lattice phase, and that same contour class now also chooses which corner receives the maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/28/code.py:29:        tall 5x4 -> maroon(9) / green(3)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/34/code.py:12:#      A maroon carrier rectangle containing accent pixels {8,5,2} is erased; a similar\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:27:      color: recolor foreground to maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:63:    - size 4 and size 5 motifs differ by obvious stroke thickness and by the size of the central maroon stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:67:    - there are only three output colors (black, orange, maroon), as in the original task\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:68:    - the maroon stamp occupies one centered block, while the lattice remains readable around it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:166:    Decode a 4x4 or 5x5 enlarged contour glyph into a larger-period orange lattice and stamp the glyph family back in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:176:    - Fill a black 28x28 canvas by repeating that phase tile, then place a 2x2 maroon copy of the original enlarged glyph at the canvas center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/800d221b/D7/1/code.py:3:# Change: hub固定为3x3实心方块... → hub为十字形\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/800d221b/D7/1/code.py:6:# - The visible difference is the core behavior change from \"hub固定为3x3实心方块\" to \"hub为十字形\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/800d221b/D7/1/code.py:8:# - Variant detail: hub不是方块，而是十字形（+形）结构。改变了hub的视觉特征和边界像素分布，分支的连接方式也相应变化。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:23:#      keeping the maroon phase glyph legible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:28:#    - Reusing the whole boolean motif as the center stamp would incorrectly recolor decoration cells to maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:37:#    - Both colors are chosen from non-special ARC colors excluding black, orange, and maroon; they are distinct.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:39:#    - Across examples, one input color controls the global orange lattice and the maroon core glyph, while the other\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:47:#    - The maroon phase stamp and the decoration layer are disjoint by construction, avoiding ambiguous overpainting.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:50:#      the phase color is interpreted structurally: its shape becomes the orange lattice code plus a maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:148:    - Tile the canonical glyph 2x2 in maroon at the center, and tile the other color's mask 2x2 as an additional\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:25:#      with the same phase decode and centered maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:44:#    - Humans can compare the edge bars with the maroon 6x6 center stamp in the output and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:53:#      orange, and maroon only. Colors are role-based and unchanged from the original\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:156:    Read a border legend that encodes a contour glyph, then expand it into the same 16x16 phase lattice and centered maroon stamp as the original task family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:166:    - Tile the phase over a black 16x16 canvas, then stamp a 2x2 maroon tiling of the reconstructed glyph into the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:169:    - The input foreground no longer marks the glyph directly inside the field; it is a border template that must be read first, and only the reconstructed motif controls both the lattice phase and the central maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/2/code.py:24:#     - output remains a 16x16 orange/black period-3 lattice with a centered 6x6 maroon stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/2/code.py:52:#       The central maroon stamp still shows the original L orientation, so the relation between\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/2/code.py:66:#     - center stamping can still overwrite the lattice safely because the maroon layer is the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/2/code.py:74:#     - the 2x2 maroon stamp exposes the source glyph directly, letting a human compare stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/2/code.py:77:#     - the task still uses three output colors only: black, orange, maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/2/code.py:79:#       legible because maroon cleanly overwrites orange/black cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/2/code.py:142:    - Repeat that orange/black phase tile across the 16x16 canvas, then stamp the original glyph tiled 2x2 in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D8/0/code.py:58:#      \"irrelevant marker\" colors, and output colors remain black/orange/maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D8/0/code.py:125:    Recover the lone valid 3x3 contour code from a noisy orange field, then build the same 16x16 phase lattice and centered maroon stamp as in the base task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D8/0/code.py:135:    - Tile the recovered 3x3 glyph 2x2 and stamp its true cells in maroon inside the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3e6067c3/16/code.py:22:#      因此会覆盖两端朝向通道的边框条带，把两个方块视觉上打通。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3e6067c3/16/code.py:52:#   和中间通道，不会穿过无关方块。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/0/code.py:17:#   shifts it by one column. The central 6x6 maroon stamp is unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/0/code.py:35:#   Phase shifts affect the whole background lattice while the central maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/0/code.py:95:    - Repeat that phase tile over a black 16x16 canvas using the chosen offset, then tile the original glyph 2x2 and recolor its true cells to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:17:#      maroon stamp made by tiling the 3x3 glyph 2x2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:33:#      leaving the centered maroon stamp unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:44:#    - The centered 6x6 maroon stamp in output is unchanged and cannot conflict with generation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:50:#    - The output still has only two clean layers: periodic background and centered maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:53:#    - Colors are unchanged from the original task: orange/black for the lattice and maroon for\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:91:    Turn the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice whose phase is shifted by the glyph placement, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:102:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3e6067c3/10/code.py:38:#    每个对象只用 3 种颜色且严格同心，桥只画在对象间背景通道里。共享的内框色与填充色让版面整齐，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3e6067c3/10/code.py:42:#    同时 outer-2 的旧单层通道宽度严格大于 core 宽度，因此桥宽变化也有可见结构证据。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:27:#      6x6 maroon stamp made by tiling the 3x3 glyph 2x2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:54:#    - Center stamping still assumes the lattice can be overwritten by maroon on motif\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:64:#    - Humans can see the change directly: outside the maroon center, orange cells now\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:72:#      centered maroon overlay. The overlay is confined to a 6x6 block, so most of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:75:#    - Output colors stay limited to black(0), orange(7), and maroon(9). Orange marks the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:77:#      maroon marks the centered 2x2 glyph stamp. This structured reuse keeps the rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:103:    Turn the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice that uses the glyph itself as the orange phase tile, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:113:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/23/code.py:3:# Name: 多色控制通道+颜色值编码尺寸\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D16/1/code.py:141:    - Fill a 16x16 canvas by tiling that phase with the legend-selected colors, then stamp a 2x2 maroon copy of the glyph in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:22:#     stamp: still a 2x2 tiling of the original glyph recolored to maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:31:#     plus -> decode phase -> always build a 16x16 lattice -> stamp the 6x6 maroon motif at rows 5..10, cols 5..10\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:33:#     plus -> decode phase -> build a 12x12 lattice -> center the same 6x6 maroon stamp at rows 3..8, cols 3..8\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:34:#     H    -> decode phase -> build an 18x18 lattice -> center the same 6x6 maroon stamp at rows 6..11, cols 6..11\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:52:#   - Output placement is always legal because every canvas size is square and >= 12, while the maroon stamp is fixed at 6x6.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:57:#   - The new rule is visible because the whole output frame expands or shrinks by glyph type while the central maroon motif stays 6x6.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:61:#   - Only three output colors remain: black, orange, maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:62:#   - The maroon stamp stays in a dedicated centered block, separated from the outer lattice by several cells on every size class.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:120:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour motif into a glyph-sized periodic lattice and place a centered maroon stamp of the motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:130:    - Fill that square canvas by tiling the decoded phase tile, then center a 2x2 maroon tiling of the original glyph on top.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3e6067c3/28/code.py:21:#   原逻辑会失败三次：它会把 7 当识别色、把 5x5 内域误作通道、并把 2->4 段画成 2。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:21:#     - the old output had one 6x6 maroon stamp at the center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:32:#     - place one 6x6 maroon plus-stamp at center top-left (5,5)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:36:#     - place the same 6x6 maroon plus-stamp four times at the quadrant-style slot origins\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:39:#     - the maroon foreground is no longer a single central event; it forms a regular 2x2 arrangement\n