hi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:38:#    - The old code assumed the only maroon overlay lived in a centered 6x6 block made by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:53:#      black, and the maroon glyph migrates to all four corners. Because the lattice still\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:58:#      center, maroon stamps only in corners. No region carries multiple competing marks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:61:#    - Colors remain black/orange/maroon only in the output. Maroon still signals the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:108:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice whose center becomes a black void and whose corners carry maroon glyph stamps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:118:    - Erase the centered 6x6 zone to pure black, then stamp one maroon copy of the glyph into each of the four 3x3 corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:178:    # corner must contain at least one maroon pixel from the glyph stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/26/code.py:33:#     - 因而同一张输出里同时出现两类证据：中带障碍保持原色并截断光束，侧带障碍内部出现青色通道。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/26/code.py:53:#     - 阻挡障碍不被覆盖，穿透障碍内部会出现整段青色通道，两类视觉结果非常干净。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D12/0/code.py:96:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 into a 6x6 pattern and recolor its true cells to maroon at the exact center of the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/25/code.py:25:#       combo: source anchors {red, teal, yellow, maroon}, destination markers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/25/code.py:27:#       solver must first notice that yellow and maroon never occur in the target and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D12/2/code.py:30:#      centered 6x6 maroon mark. Empty input cells map to all-black panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D12/2/code.py:59:#    - Panels are spatially disjoint, separated by black gutters, and maroon only appears\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D12/2/code.py:158:    - In the output mosaic, fill the corresponding 8x8 panel with that orange/black tile and stamp a 2x2 tiling of the glyph in maroon at the panel center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:20:#     old_center_rule: every true pixel of the 2x2 tiled glyph became maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:21:#     new_center_rule: maroon appears only where the tiled glyph overlaps the 3-period lattice seams\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:25:#     variant: for plus, only the 8 true pixels on rows {0,3} or cols {0,3} inside that 6x6 box become maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:29:#       which would collapse the stamp to zero maroon pixels\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:101:    - Tile the 3x3 glyph 2x2 into the centered 6x6 box, but recolor to maroon only where those glyph pixels also lie on the box's period-3 seam rows or seam columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:126:    maroon_mask = center & seam_mask\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:130:    out[r0 : r0 + center.shape[0], c0 : c0 + center.shape[1]][maroon_mask] = Color.MAROON\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:149:    maroon_count = int((center == Color.MAROON).sum())\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:150:    if maroon_count <= 0:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/4/code.py:14:      in the center window with fixed maroon(9). This variant transfers the visible input\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/4/code.py:20:    - Original behavior at the last step: center glyph pixels become maroon regardless of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/4/code.py:60:      maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d8