ode.py:23:#       travel around that annulus, and then find the next opening before reaching farther maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:36:#       a single-stage outer barrier, and the closest reachable maroons were collected first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:38:#       maroons beyond more frames are the intended targets and are filled before nearer annulus maroons. Those far sources are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:40:#       maroons are actually pulled into the destination block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:46:#     - The BFS passable set {floor, maroon} also remains correct. Nested frames change connectivity, not the movement rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:52:#     - Each generated input includes reachable maroons at multiple frame depths, with at least one moved source beyond the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:53:#       outermost frame. The user can see that some maroons sit after one gate while others sit beyond two or three gates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:64:    Pull the nearest reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:68:    - Magenta pixels now form 2 or 3 nested rectangular frames, each with its own opening, and maroon pixels are scattered on floor cells at different frame depths.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:71:    - Start from passable cells next to the target block and flood-fill through orange and maroon cells only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:72:    - Any maroon reached through the chain of frame openings is a candidate; maroons that lie deeper behind the nested gates are prioritized ahead of nearer annulus maroons, with row/column used to break ties.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:73:    - The chosen maroons are removed from their old positions and replaced by the floor color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:75:    Key insight: The transformation is still a reachability task, but nested frame openings now do double duty: they determine which maroons are reachable at all, and they stratify reachable maroons by traversal depth so the outermost successful targets are collected first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:139:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:140:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:141:    # Nested-frame variants should favor maroons that lie behind more gates, which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:143:    maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:145:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:146:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:214:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:215:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:216:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:218:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:219:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D16/2/code.py:3:# Change: 禁止角切割——对角线移动时，两个正交中间格子都必须在区域内，否则无法通过... → 宽度约束（需要2格宽通道）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D1/0/code.py:43:#     - 原 solver 把 `passable={floor,9}`，意味着 maroon 也可作为通道；变体中 maroon 反而应该终止视线，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D1/0/code.py:60:#     - solver 假设颜色固定为 floor=7, wall=6, dest=3, center=2, maroon=9；生成器固定满足。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D1/0/code.py:167:    Move the closest directly visible maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D1/0/code.py:170:    - Orange floor surrounds a fixed green 3×3 block with one red center, plus optional magenta wall cells and scattered maroon pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D1/0/code.py:175:    - That first blocking cell counts as a candidate only when it is maroon. Rank all such candidates by ray distance, then by row and column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D1/0/code.py:176:    - Move the closest candidates into the destination block in row-major order, erasing only the maroon sources that were selected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D1/0/code.py:179:    - Reachability is no longer about turning through corridors. A maroon pixel can be topologically connected through the floor yet still remain untouched if it is not the first thing seen on a straight ray from the green block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D1/0/code.py:304:    # Ensure these added maroons stay off the direct rays.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:17:#    - `maroons.sort()` 依赖的是“最近优先”；这是唯一必须替换的 solver 关键行，改为按距离降序排序。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:18:#    - `chosen = maroons[:k]` 在新排序下仍合法，因为 k 的意义不变，只是候选序列顺序改变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:105:def _reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[list[tuple[int, int]], int, list[tuple[int, int, int]]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:120:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:122:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:123:    return dest_cells, floor, maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:128:    Move the farthest reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block centered on the lone red cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:131:    - The board is an orange floor with optional magenta walls and scattered maroon source pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:135:    - Flood-fill outward from cells touching the destination, walking only through floor or maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:136:    - Only reachable maroon pixels are eligible, and they are ranked by distance from far to near before filling destination cells in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:140:    - The walls still decide which maroon pixels belong to the same reachable region, but unlike the original task the destination prefers the outermost reachable tokens first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:145:    dest_cells, floor, maroons = _reachable_maroons(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:147:    maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))  # farthest first; ties stay row-major\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:149:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:150:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:391:        _, _, maroons = _reachable_maroons(inp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:392:        ordered_asc = sorted(maroons)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:393:        ordered_desc = sorted(maroons, key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:22:#      orange floor, optional magenta walls, and scattered maroon tokens.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:23:#    - Connectivity still comes from flood-fill through floor/maroon cells starting at passable cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:25:#    - The changed step is only the ranking of reachable maroons. In the original task, if reachable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:26:#      maroons were at (1,8),(2,2),(8,1),(9,9) with distances 1,5,3,2, the chosen order was by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:30:#    - If the number of reachable maroons is <= 9, every reachable maroon moves and the new ranking\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:32:#      maroons, so only 9 move and some remain behind.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:38:#      non-maroon non-destination cell remains visible. The generator therefore reserves at least one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:40:#    - BFS reachability through {floor, maroon} remains valid because D3 changes only ranking, not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:42:#    - The original `maroons.sort()` encoded the old dimension directly. That line must change to sort\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:45:#    - Source maroons are sampled only from reachable floor cells outside the 3x3 destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:47:#      destination cells, or source maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:52:#    - With >9 reachable maroons, the output shows a full 3x3 maroon block plus leftover maroons whose\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:56:#    - Walls still separate reachable from unreachable zones, so moved vs unmoved maroons are spatially\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:59:#    - No new color mapping is introduced. The only colors stay red/green/orange/magenta/maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:117:    asser