le[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D17/0/code.py:158:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D17/0/code.py:160:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D17/0/code.py:161:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/0/code.py:10:#   walls and scattered maroon tokens.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/0/code.py:11:# - The original task sorted reachable maroon tokens by BFS distance and then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/0/code.py:23:#   so the task is still \"collect nearest reachable maroons through corridors\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/0/code.py:40:# - Source maroons remain on floor cells outside the destination and walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/0/code.py:60:#   destination and at least k reachable maroon placements can be selected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/0/code.py:93:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/0/code.py:96:    - The canvas is mostly orange floor, sometimes split by magenta wall barriers, with scattered maroon tokens.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/0/code.py:100:    - Maroon tokens reachable from the destination through floor/maroon cells are ranked by BFS distance, with row/col tie-breaks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/0/code.py:104:    Key insight: The hard part is still the flood-fill reachability through wall-made corridors, but once the valid maroons are chosen, the destination path is a mirrored fill that grows from bottom-right toward top-left.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/0/code.py:126:    assert cand_ring, \"ring around destination must contain passable (non-maroon, non-red, non-wall) cells to infer floor color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D