er uses the same maroon color as the head but much smaller shape, keeping the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D11/1/code.py:62:# - Color semantics are unchanged from the original task: maroon marks head/target, grey is charge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D11/1/code.py:133:    The head is still a full maroon line on one side of the container. The destination is now a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D11/1/code.py:134:    single maroon point farther along the movement axis. Translation distance is measured from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D11/2/code.py:3:# Change: 头部和目标线形状完全相同（同长度的水平或垂直线段），颜色相同（maroon/9）... → 目标线为L形或T形\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D11/2/code.py:22:#      maroon L or T marker placed farther along the movement axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D11/2/code.py:57:#    - The change is visible: the maroon target is no longer a straight line,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D11/2/code.py:66:#      maroon, so the variant stays within ARC's visible reasoning regime.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D11/2/code.py:68:#    - Every container has exactly one adjacent maroon head line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D11/2/code.py:69:#    - Every destination marker is a separate maroon component and is either:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/1/code.py:20:#   containers, grey/orange interior, and a maroon head-line flush with one container side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/1/code.py:21:# - Movers still have a same-shaped maroon destination line farther along the head direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/1/code.py:25:#   for a matching maroon line above it and move upward by min(distance, 3). In the variant,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/1/code.py:42:# - The fix is to treat only non-border-adjacent maroon components as external destinations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/1/code.py:74:# - Heads must remain the only maroon pixels adjacent to their own border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/3/code.py:30:      * no_head decoy: the border+interior exists, a distant maroon target line\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/3/code.py:31:        exists on one side, but the 1-cell-thick maroon line adjacent to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/3/code.py:34:        maroon head/dest lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/3/code.py:51:      maroon markers, preventing ambiguous head/destination pairing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/2/code.py:40:#     - obstacle 只放在本容器的通道里，因此最近的同形 dest 仍唯一可配对。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D14/1/code.py:3:# Change: 每个周期位置涂1个像素——涂点是单个格子... → 涂色扩展为十字形\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D14/1/code.py:41:# - 十字形落色只发生在扩展侧，且对每个候选格单独做边界检查与背景检查，因此不会越界，也不会覆盖\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D14/1/code.py:43:# - 生成器仍采用 output-first：先放条形，再按 solver 同步的顺序模拟十字形扩展，最后清空扩展侧\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D14/1/code.py:57:#   “十字形会往上下多染 1 格”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:21:#    {(8,8),(7,8),(9,8),(8,7),(8,9)}=1. Sprite hits and lone bg landings stay maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:25:#    least one lone bg landing, so each sample contains both a blue cross and a maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:45:#    least one maroon lone landing in the same sample makes the branching rule inferable:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:46:#    one projectile on empty bg -> maroon point, multiple projectiles on empty bg -> blue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:53:#    Only two effect colors remain relevant: maroon for lone bg hits / hit sprites, blue for\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:145:    - A landing on an existing sprite recolors the whole struck sprite to maroon (9), and a lone landing on empty background paints only that landing cell maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:183:    # Projectile hitting a sprite recolors the entire sprite to maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:188:    # Projectile landings on empty background: lone impacts are maroon, repeated impacts explode into a blue cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D4/0/code.py:18:#    - input: left red lane has two maroon sprites, green lane has one blue sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D4/0/code.py:20:#    - variant output: green lane keeps its bottom blue sprite, and the two newly filled slots above are maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/1/code.py:36:#       1/2/3 and keeps maroon(9) recolors visibly meaningful.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/1/code.py:54:#     - Many samples also include a lone maroon landing or a maroon sprite-hit, so the viewer can contrast\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/1/code.py:159:    Triangular sprites launch 5-cell projectiles; sprite hits stay maroon while empty-cell collisions are count-colored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/1/code.py:168:    - If a landing cell lies on a sprite, recolor the entire hit sprite to maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/1/code.py:169:    - If a landing cell is empty background, paint that one cell according to how many projectiles arrived there: 1 projectile -> maroon (9), 2 -> blue (1), 3 -> red (2), 4 -> green (3), then continue through the visible non-background palette while skipping the background color 7.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:3:# Change: 单一矩形灰色框架，框架线条均匀，内部为操作区域... → 框架为非矩形（L形或十字形）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/2/code.py:34:#         (0,1)->(1,0), (1,1)->(1,-1), etc. The visible change is the maroon trail after X.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/2/code.py:59:#       lone maroon landing dots or sprite recolors, so the user can isolate the changed branch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/2/code.py:337:    Key insight: Sprite orientation still determines the first rendezvous point, but a shared empty landing is no longer the final output mark; it is a right-angle redirection hub whose outgoing maroon trail reveals the new rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D9/0/code.py:27:      - original rule: yellow target becomes maroon 9\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D9/1/code.py:14:#        * 1 projectile -> maroon 9 (unchanged from the source task)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D9/1/code.py:16:#        * >=2 projectiles, mixed teams -> maroon 9\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D9/1/code.py:18:#        * an enemy-team projectile recolors the whole hit sprite to maroon 9\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D9/1/code.py:24:#        * Variant: now maroon, because the collision is cross-team.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D9/1/code.py:25:#        * Original: red sprite A hits red sprite B => B turns maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D9/1/code.py:33:#      This forces a visible contrast between blue and maroon collision markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D9/1/code.py:42:#    - Original bg rule `if len(shooters) >= 2: blue else maroon` assumed collision outcome depends\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D9/1/code.py:56:#      blue-vs-maroon difference can be compared within a single grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D9/1/code.py:162:    - If a projectile lands on a sprite of the opposite team, that whole target sprite becomes maroon (9); same-team hits do nothing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D9/1/code.py:163:    - If projectiles land on an empty background cell, a same-team collision paints blue (1), while a mixed-team collision paints maroon (9); a lone projectile also paints maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D9/1/code.py:166:    - Orientation still determines where each projectile goes, but color now determines what a shared landing means: same team cooperates into blue, opposite teams clash into maroon, and only enemy fire damages a sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:19:#   (5), while every sprite that gets hit is recolored to maroon (9). Empty landing cells still\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:20:#   follow the old rule: one projectile -> maroon (9), two or more -> blue (1).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:25:#   fired and stayed safe, while C becomes maroon because it was hit. The bg landing markers are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:36:#   overwrite maroon hit sprites, so hit recoloring happens after safe recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:42:#   To keep the new recolor rule readable, initial sprite colors exclude grey (5) and maroon (9),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:50:#   Only three output marker colors carry meaning: grey=safe shooter, maroon=hit sprite or lone bg\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:54:#   main() now assumes any component it recolors grey or maroon is a valid 3-cell triangle detected\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:129:    - Any sprite that is hit by at least one projectile is recolored maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:132:      maroon (9) for a single projectile.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:136:      states: safe shooters become grey, while struck sprites become maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/1/code.py:21:#     - a shared empty-bg landing still becomes blue(1); a lone landing is maroon(9)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/1/code.py:23:#     - ori